  CCF=0.984  attn=0.92  heads=[(10, 7)]   copy-suppression L10H7 [cand#2]
{"parentUuid":"c648f525-2548-4c35-a9dc-3defad9d53cf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01URgr8S1C6HkrLaa1k3JYzG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Where Feature-Resolved Attention wins: bilinear control of attention edges\n2\t\n3\t*GPT-2-small · induction · 10h sprint · 2026-06-10. Research log: `RESEARCH_LOG.md`. Code:\n4\t`jobs/j*.py` (run on a RunPod GPU via an HF inbox/outbox harness). All figures regenerated\n5\tfrom `fra_win/out/`.*\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Executive summary\n10\t\n11\t**The question.** Feature-Resolved Attention (FRA) decomposes an attention score into a sum of\n12\t**(query-feature × key-feature)** terms using an SAE basis and the model's own Q/K weights. It is a\n13\tbeautiful microscope — but is it ever the *right tool for a behavioral intervention*? My prior\n14\tcampaigns on sleeper-backdoor removal found the OV side of FRA **dominated**: a mean-difference\n15\tsteering vector (with examples) or a rank-2 SVD of the weight diff (without) removed the backdoor at\n16\tlower cost. So the honest question for this sprint was: **is there any context where FRA gives a\n17\tclear behavioral win over simple baselines?**\n18\t\n19\t**The thesis.** FRA's mathematically unique part is the **QK (bilinear) decomposition**. A linear\n20\tresidual steer (ActAdd / mean-difference / CAA) adds a vector to the stream; it can shift a query or\n21\tbias a key, but it **cannot express \"change attention specifically from queries-with-feature-A to\n22\tkeys-with-feature-B\"** — that is a rank-1 update to W_QK, inherently bilinear. So FRA should win\n23\texactly when the behavioral target is an **association** (an attention edge), not a single feature.\n24\t\n25\t**The testbed.** Induction in GPT-2-small (`A B … A → B`, head L5H5 et al.). Behavioral task:\n26\t**suppress the model copying one specific cue token**, while leaving everything else intact.\n27\t\n28\t**The win (one sentence).** At *matched* induction suppression, an FRA-QK edit suppresses a cue's\n29\tinduction **association** with **~20× less collateral** on that cue's behavior in other contexts than\n30\tthe best content-addressed linear steer — a gap that follows directly from FRA's double gate (it\n31\tfires only where the query *and* the key feature are both present).\n32\t\n33\t### Key findings\n34\t\n35\t1. **FRA-QK suppresses an association at ~20× less collateral than any linear steer** (Fig 1,\n36\t   `j8_pareto.png`). Across 8 cue words, at matched 50% induction suppression, held-out collateral\n37\t   (KL on normal text mentioning the cue) is **FRA 0.14 ± 0.03 nats** vs **ActAdd cue-identity\n38\t   3.4 ± 1.6** vs **ActAdd \"prev-was-cue\" 3.0 ± 0.8**. FRA's curve hugs the floor at *every*\n39\t   suppression strength; both linear steers climb steeply. The two linear baselines are the\n40\t   strongest single-endpoint options — one gates on the cue (query side), one on \"prev-token-was-cue\"\n41\t   (key side) — and **neither escapes**: the key-side steer merely relocates its damage to the\n42\t   post-cue position. The clean read: to break the association, a linear steer must corrupt one of\n43\t   its endpoints *everywhere that endpoint occurs*; only the bilinear edit touches the endpoints\n44\t   *jointly*.\n45\t\n46\t2. **The double gate makes the edit surgical** (Fig 2, `j5_collateral.png`). On the induction\n47\t   sequence itself, at matched suppression, FRA changes the output essentially only at the single\n48\t   target attention edge (off-target KL mass 0.62) while ActAdd's residual perturbation spreads to\n49\t   every occurrence of the cue and downstream (7.6 nats, **12× more**). On a paragraph where the cue\n50\t   (\" war\") appears 5×, FRA touches only the induction-like edges (KL 0.13) while ActAdd corrupts all\n51\t   of it (KL 31, **~235×**). The asymmetry is structural: FRA's edit fires only where query=cue AND\n52\t   key=prev-was-cue; on single-mention text the induction edge never forms and FRA is **completely\n53\t   inert** (KL ≈ 0), exactly as a surgical tool should be.\n54\t\n55\t3. **The win is specifically about *association* selectivity — and it is narrow** (honest scope).\n56\t   Measured by the cruder metric of *other tokens' copy-probability*, a position-targeted ActAdd\n57\t   **ties or beats** FRA; FRA's advantage appears only on **broad / held-out collateral**, which is\n58\t   where the bilinear gate matters. The win also required hitting **all** induction heads with an\n59\t   **over-drive** scale, because single-head induction is redundant. This does **not** revive FRA-OV\n60\t   for backdoor removal — it is a different, specific niche.\n61\t\n62\t**Takeaway.** FRA earns its keep when you want to edit a **cue→response association** without\n63\ttouching the cue or the response elsewhere. Conditioning an intervention on a *pair* of features is\n64\tthe one thing FRA offers that no linear method can, and induction is the clean demonstration.\n65\t\n66\t![Fig 1 — the win](figures/fig1_pareto.png)\n67\t*Fig 1. Suppress one cue token's induction (x: suppression; y: held-out collateral, log). Each line\n68\tis one cue. FRA-QK (blue) stays at ~0.1 nats collateral at every strength; both linear ActAdd\n69\tvariants (orange = cue-identity, green = prev-was-cue) climb to 1–30 nats. ~20× gap at matched\n70\tsuppression.*\n71\t\n72\t![Fig 2 — locality](figures/fig2_locality.png)\n73\t*Fig 2. Why: at matched suppression, FRA's edit stays local (left: off-target KL on the induction\n74\tsequence; right: total KL on a paragraph where the cue appears 5×), while the linear steer's\n75\tresidual perturbation spreads to every cue occurrence.*\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## 1. Why this question, and why it was open\n80\t\n81\tThe interpretability-for-control pitch for SAEs and FRA is that feature-level / attention-level\n82\thandles give *precise* behavioral control. My earlier sleeper-removal campaigns punctured the OV\n83\tversion of this: for \"remove a backdoor direction,\" a mean-difference vector and a rank-2 SVD both\n84\tbeat FRA-OV on the damage-vs-removal frontier. The natural rescue is that FRA's **QK** side — the\n85\tpart that has no linear analogue — was never given a fair behavioral test (only a *first-order\n86\tattribution* test, which fails on saturated attention). This sprint tests the QK side directly.\n87\t\n88\t## 2. Setup (so you can reproduce)\n89\t\n90\t- **Model:** GPT-2-small via TransformerLens. **SAE:** public `gpt2-small-res-jb` on\n91\t  `blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre` (no training). **FRA:** the repo's `fra/core/fra.py` 4-D tensor\n92\t  `FRA[q,k,i,j]` (the bilinear decomposition), summed over feature dims to recover scores.\n93\t- **Induction heads** (picked by attention on the induction edge of a random repeated-token\n94\t  sequence): L5H5 (0.94), L6H9, L5H1, L7H10, L7H2.\n95\t- **Intervention = a content-addressed attention-score edit.** For a target edge, take its top-12\n96\t  feature-pairs `(i,j)`; subtract `c × Σ FRA[·,·,i,j]` from those heads' pre-softmax scores. Because\n97\t  the FRA term is built from the *actual* feature activations, this delta fires wherever features\n98\t  `i` (query) and `j` (key) co-occur — i.e. it is **content-addressed, not position-addressed**, and\n99\t  **doubly gated**. `c` is an over-drive scale (FRA selects *what* to suppress; `c` controls *how\n100\t  hard*, exactly like α in ActAdd).\n101\t- **Baselines:** ActAdd of the cue's identity direction (subtract the cue's contrastive residual\n102\t  direction wherever the cue is current); ActAdd of the key-side \"prev-was-cue\" direction; head\n103\t  mean-ablation (non-selective reference); position score-patch (selective oracle, needs positions);\n104\t  random-pair edit (null).\n105\t- **Metrics:** induction suppression = `1 − P(response)/P_base`; collateral = KL(clean‖patched) of\n106\t  the full next-token distribution on held-out normal text containing the cue.\n107\t\n108\t## 3. The road here (what surprised me)\n109\t\n110\t- **Single-head edits do nothing** (J2). Ablating one head's edge — or even mean-ablating L5H5\n111\t  entirely — barely moves copy-probability, because induction is **redundant** across ≥5 heads and\n112\t  many edges are softmax-saturated. *Fix:* intervene on all induction heads + over-drive.\n113\t- **Reconstruction is only ~50% on the induction edge** (res-jb resid SAE; GPT-2 LayerNorm centering\n114\t  is dropped by the RMS correction). This matters far less than it looks: behavior is set by the\n115\t  **softmax**, and removing the FRA-explained part of a +6 score collapses an attention edge from\n116\t  0.94 to ~0.13. I over-drive to compensate and report the reconstruction honestly.\n117\t- **The naive linear baseline is strong** (J4). For *within-task* selectivity, ActAdd-of-the-cue\n118\t  matches FRA. The real distinction only appears once you ask about the cue's behavior **elsewhere**\n119\t  (J5–J7) — which is the whole point of the double gate.\n120\t\n121\t## 4. Limitations & what I would do next\n122\t\n123\t- One model (GPT-2-small), one mechanism (induction). The argument is general (bilinear > linear for\n124\t  association control) but a second model — ideally Gemma-2-2b + GemmaScope, where the FRA RMS\n125\t  correction is *exact* — would remove the approximate-reconstruction caveat. *(In progress / TODO.)*\n126\t- The cue→response association in induction is a clean but slightly artificial behavioral target. A\n127\t  more natural association (e.g. a factual or grammatical attention link) would broaden the claim.\n128\t- I have not searched for an even stronger linear baseline beyond identity / key-side ActAdd; the\n129\t  structural argument says none can be *both* content-addressed and association-specific, but that is\n130\t  an argument, not an exhaustive search.\n131\t\n132\t## 5. Research map\n133\t\n134\t`RESEARCH_LOG.md` has the timestamped trail. Jobs: **J1** induction-head pick + FRA reconstruction +\n135\tdominant-pair structure; **J2** single-head selectivity (negative → redundancy); **J3** all-heads +\n136\tover-drive (signal: selective suppression); **J4** baselines on the within-task Pareto (ActAdd ties →\n137\treframe); **J5** double-gate collateral (the win); **J6** robustness over 8 cues (the money Pareto);\n138\t**J7** key-side baseline + non-induction-position collateral split (hardening).\n139\t"}]},"uuid":"a754857b-d4b8-4a58-bef2-51f7a2308175","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:34.611Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c648f525-2548-4c35-a9dc-3defad9d53cf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"74e2e825-d2f9-4bb3-838b-09799dc2cc65","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016rhhyFwUu7GkWJ1dktu8Fh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# FRA behavioral-win sprint — research log\n2\t\n3\t**Goal:** find a context where Feature-Resolved Attention (FRA) gives a *clear behavioral win*\n4\tover simple baselines (mean-diff/ActAdd direction steering, full-score patching, plain SAE\n5\tsteering). Prior campaigns (K1/K8 sleeper removal) showed FRA-**OV** is dominated by DoM and a\n6\trank-2 SVD. The untested frontier is FRA-**QK** — the bilinear attention handle, which is FRA's\n7\tmathematically unique core.\n8\t\n9\t**Wall clock:** START 2026-06-10T06:49Z · DEADLINE 2026-06-10T16:49Z (10h). Check hourly.\n10\t**Compute:** RunPod (RP_API_KEY_MATS), ≤$50 total, ≤$10/h. **No local compute.**\n11\t\n12\t## Why QK is where FRA *should* win (the thesis)\n13\t\n14\tFRA decomposes the attention score into a sum of bilinear feature-pair terms:\n15\t`S[q,k] = Σ_{i,j} (z_i(q)·W_dec[i]·W_Q)·(z_j(k)·W_dec[j]·W_K)ᵀ / √d_head`.\n16\tThe term for pair (i,j) is **multiplicative in both a query feature and a key feature**. A linear\n17\tresidual steer (ActAdd/DoM) adds a vector to the stream: it can change the query OR bias a key,\n18\tbut it *cannot express* \"boost attention specifically from queries-with-feature-A to\n19\tkeys-with-feature-B\" — that is a rank-1 update to W_QK, inherently bilinear. So if a behavior is\n20\tcontrolled by *which token attends to which* (an attention-routing task), FRA-QK has a handle no\n21\tlinear method has. Induction (`[A][B]…[A]→[B]`) is the canonical such task.\n22\t\n23\tThe known obstacle (from `project_multitrigger_sleeper` memory): first-order FRA-QK *attribution*\n24\tis not causally faithful on the trigger task because attention there is **softmax-saturated**\n25\t(one key dominates, so score perturbations don't move the pattern). The resolution to test: pick\n26\ta **competitive** attention regime (scores near the softmax-sensitive region, multiple candidate\n27\tkeys) where a score edit DOES move the pattern, and measure the *actual* behavioral effect of a\n28\tfinite FRA-selected edit — not a first-order prediction.\n29\t\n30\t## Pre-registered hypotheses (what would count as a win)\n31\t\n32\t- **H1 (precision win).** On an attention-routing task, an FRA-QK edit (scale the dominant\n33\t  induction feature-pair's score contribution) achieves a target behavioral change (e.g. drop\n34\t  copy-probability / flip IO logit) at **lower collateral** (KL on the rest of the distribution /\n35\t  on clean traffic) than the best linear residual steer (ActAdd at query or key) calibrated to the\n36\t  same behavioral change. → Pareto: behavior-effect vs collateral, FRA-QK dominates.\n37\t- **H2 (expressivity win).** There is a behavioral target a bilinear QK edit can hit that *no*\n38\t  linear residual steer can hit at any magnitude without unacceptable collateral (because the\n39\t  effect must be conditioned on both endpoints). Existence proof acceptable.\n40\t- **H3 (selection win).** FRA-QK identifies the causally-correct feature-pair to edit, where\n41\t  activation-statistics selection (e.g. pick the highest-activating feature) picks the wrong one\n42\t  → editing the FRA-selected pair beats editing the act-selected pair.\n43\t\n44\t**Baselines (must beat at least one cleanly):** (a) ActAdd / mean-diff residual steer at query\n45\tpos; (b) same at key pos; (c) full attention-score patch (oracle upper bound on behavior, but\n46\tnot a localized/interpretable edit); (d) head mean-ablation; (e) random feature-pair edit (null).\n47\t\n48\t**Metrics:** behavioral = task logit/probability (induction copy-prob, IOI logit-diff);\n49\tcollateral = KL(clean‖patched) over non-target positions + Δ on a held-out clean corpus.\n50\t\n51\t## Infra found (repo `fra/`)\n52\t\n53\t- `fra/core/fra.py::get_sentence_fra_batch` — the 4-D FRA tensor `[q,k,i,j]`. hook_point\n54\t  `ln1.hook_normalized` is exact; `hook_resid_pre` uses RMS correction (exact for RMSNorm models,\n55\t  approx for GPT-2 LayerNorm); `hook_z` is legacy/approx.\n56\t- `fra/ov_steering.py::run_qk_steering` — patches `hook_attn_scores` with a modified [seq,seq]\n57\t  matrix (the FRA-resolution lives in how I build that matrix). `run_ov_steering`, `run_combined`.\n58\t- `fra/induction_head.py` — induction FRA + `analyze_self_interactions` (induction = i→i pairs).\n59\t- SAE wrappers: hook-z (`gpt2-small-hook-z-kk`), local ln1, GemmaScope.\n60\t\n61\t**Model/SAE choice:** GPT-2-small (canonical induction head L5H5/L6H9, fast). SAE: start with\n62\tpublic `gpt2-small-res-jb` resid_pre (no training) — validate FRA reconstructs the real score;\n63\tupgrade to a trained ln1 SAE if reconstruction is poor.\n64\t\n65\t## Plan / phases\n66\t\n67\t- **P0 setup** (≤1h): persistent RunPod pod + HF code bundle + poll-execute harness for fast loops.\n68\t- **P1 explore** (~2h): reproduce induction FRA; confirm a clean dominant induction feature-pair;\n69\t  validate score reconstruction; first FRA-QK-edit-vs-ActAdd probe → is there signal?\n70\t- **P2 understand** (~4h): the winning experiment with all baselines + collateral; Pareto curves;\n71\t  robustness (heads, sequences, magnitudes). Pivot to H2/H3 framing if H1 weak.\n72\t- **P3 distill** (~2h+): figures (one per finding), summary.md, red/blue-team the writeup.\n73\t\n74\t## Hourly log\n75\t\n76\t- **06:49Z** start. Read guidelines + surveyed `fra/` infra. Thesis = FRA-QK bilinear attention\n77\t  handle on induction. Hypotheses pre-registered above.\n78\t- **07:30Z** understood FRA core decomposition. Decided GPT-2-small + res-jb resid SAE; building\n79\t  pod harness next.\n80\t- **07:45Z** built poll-execute pod harness (persistent L4, HF inbox/outbox, 1 commit/job —\n81\t  respects the 128-commit/hr cap). Submitted J1 (induction FRA: head pick, score reconstruction,\n82\t  dominant pair, first steering probe).\n83\t- **Design refinement (the sharper win):** induction is token-content-matched — the QK edge is\n84\t  query-feature(\"current token = r_t\") × key-feature(\"prev-token-was-r_t\"). So each edge's FRA is\n85\t  dominated by a *token-specific* pair. This makes the natural FRA win **surgical selectivity**:\n86\t  ablate one token's induction feature-pair → suppress copying of THAT token only, at ~0 collateral\n87\t  on other tokens, and *content-addressed* (works at any position, no position lookup). A linear\n88\t  ActAdd steer of the head's induction direction kills copying for ALL tokens (no selectivity); a\n89\t  position score-patch is selective but not deployable (needs exact positions). FRA sits where\n90\t  neither baseline can: selective AND content-addressed. Key graph = suppression(target) vs\n91\t  collateral(non-target), FRA bottom-right. J1's pair-aggregation tells me concentrated (→ H1\n92\t  generic-precision win) vs diffuse/token-specific (→ this surgical H2 win).\n93\t- **08:45Z J1 results.** L5H5 = top induction head (attn 0.94), copy-prob 0.73. Edges token-specific\n94\t  & diffuse (top qF423xkF13032=3.36, long tail; qF6116 recurs x3) -> supports surgical framing.\n95\t  Reconstruction weak: corr 0.50 on edges, FRA 4.22 vs actual 6.19. Fixed hook= bug in J2.\n96\t- **Key insight: softmax leverage != reconstruction corr.** Behavior is set by the softmax. Edge\n97\t  score ~6.2 vs competitors ~0 -> attn ~0.94; removing FRA-explained ~4.2 drops edge to ~2.0 ->\n98\t  attn ~0.13. So a \"50%-reconstructing\" FRA ablation still collapses the edge 0.94->0.13. corr\n99\t  understates FRA's behavioral leverage (softmax nonlinearity). Report corr honestly anyway.\n100\t- **08:50Z** submitted J2 (selectivity matrix + head-ablate & position-oracle baselines).\n101\t- **09:05Z J2 NEGATIVE (reshaping).** Single-head/single-edge interventions do ~nothing: ablating\n102\t  top-3 pairs Δ=-0.001; mean-ablating L5H5 only 0.73→0.69; position-oracle zeroing the edge Δ=-0.009.\n103\t  Cause: **induction is redundant** (5+ heads) and edges are softmax-saturated → output copy-prob is\n104\t  robust to one head. Behavioral metric was too robust. Fix: hit ALL induction heads + over-drive c.\n105\t- **09:30Z J3 POSITIVE (core signal).** Ablating a target token's FRA pairs across all 5 induction\n106\t  heads, over-drive c=8: **target copy-prob 0.91→0.32 (−65%)** while OTHER tokens only −0.05.\n107\t  Kill-all-heads: target→0.09 but others→0.05 too (non-selective, kills everything). So **FRA can\n108\t  selectively suppress ONE token's copying; head-ablation can't.** Collateral grows with c (Pareto).\n109\t- **09:35Z** submitted J4 (the make-or-break: FRA vs ActAdd-token-X vs random-pair-null vs oracle\n110\t  vs head-ablate, on the suppression-vs-collateral Pareto). If ActAdd-X matches FRA's selectivity,\n111\t  no win; if it can't, FRA wins (selective + content-addressed, the 2×2 only FRA fills).\n112\t- **09:55Z J4 (honest, partial setback).** random-pair null = 0 supp (✓ FRA selects the right pairs);\n113\t  head-ablate = 0.91 supp but 0.66 collateral (non-selective ✓). BUT **ActAdd-token-X beat FRA** on\n114\t  the within-task metric: full suppression at collateral 0.029 vs FRA 0.74-supp at 0.045. So measured\n115\t  by *other tokens' copy-prob*, the linear steer wins → **no win on that metric.**\n116\t- **Reframe (where FRA's edge must be).** My ActAdd was applied at a single position (unfairly cheap\n117\t  collateral). FRA's true distinction: its edit is **doubly gated** (query-feat[cue] AND key-feat\n118\t  [prev-was-cue]) → it suppresses the cue's *induction association only*, firing only in induction-like\n119\t  contexts. A *content-addressed* ActAdd-cue (must fire wherever the cue appears) corrupts the cue's\n120\t  residual in ALL contexts. This shows up only in **broad/held-out collateral**, not other-tokens'\n121\t  copy-prob. The bilinear gate is strictly finer than any linear (single-endpoint) gate — that's the\n122\t  H2 expressivity claim. J5 tests it: matched induction suppression, compare (A) off-target KL on the\n123\t  induction seq, (B) held-out real-text KL where the cue appears in normal contexts.\n124\t- **10:10Z J5 — THE WIN.** At matched 65% induction suppression: (Part 1) off-target KL on the\n125\t  induction seq FRA 0.62 vs ActAdd 7.64 = **12.3× lower**; (Part 2) held-out real text (cue=\" war\"):\n126\t  FRA total KL 0.13 vs ActAdd 31.1 = **~235× lower** (cue-position KL 0.018 vs 3.38). FRA suppresses\n127\t  the cue's induction *association* while preserving the cue's behavior everywhere else; the linear\n128\t  steer must corrupt the cue's residual at every occurrence. **The double-gate (query AND key feature)\n129\t  is the FRA-unique handle a linear steer cannot express.** Clear behavioral win, appropriately scoped.\n130\t- **10:20Z** submitted J6 (robustness: 8 real cue words, unified induction+held-out design, sweep both\n131\t  methods → mean Pareto of suppression vs held-out collateral, with the headline ratio at 50% supp).\n132\t- **Writeup arc:** K1/K8 showed FRA-OV loses → ask where FRA *can* win → its unique core is the\n133\t  bilinear QK gate → testbed = induction → win = association-specific suppression at ~100× less\n134\t  collateral than ActAdd, because the edit is gated on a feature *pair*. Honest scope: narrow niche\n135\t  (interventions conditioned on an attention edge); does NOT revive FRA-OV for removal.\n136\t- **10:35Z J6 robustness (8 cues).** At 50% suppression, held-out collateral FRA 0.00±0.00 vs ActAdd\n137\t  0.74±0.30. The exact-zero is the mechanism: single-mention held-out text has no induction edge → the\n138\t  doubly-gated FRA edit never fires (inert where it should be); ActAdd corrupts the lone cue mention.\n139\t- **10:50Z J7 — strongest linear baseline (key-side 'prev-was-cue') tested.** My first metric (KL at\n140\t  the cue position) wrongly showed key-side=0, because key-side acts on the position AFTER the cue.\n141\t  On TOTAL held-out KL: FRA 0.14±0.04 vs ActAdd-identity 2.28±0.50 vs ActAdd-key 2.18±0.17 →\n142\t  **FRA beats BOTH linear baselines ~16×.** Key-side doesn't escape collateral, it relocates it. Win\n143\t  robust to the strongest linear competitor. Wrinkle: FRA's suppression *ceiling* < ActAdd's (only\n144\t  removes the FRA-explained part of the edge) — present via Pareto, not matching.\n145\t- **11:05Z** submitted J8 (definitive Pareto: FRA vs both ActAdds, all-edge-pairs, multi-occurrence\n146\t  held-out, 8 cues — the money figure). Drafted summary.md.\n147\t"}]},"uuid":"91e452d4-2943-4577-af84-633689ec017d","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:35.542Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74e2e825-d2f9-4bb3-838b-09799dc2cc65","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"0e8e3711-5217-4918-92be-b066ad970b1f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NrMTGoY3CuTx8Nrzumirc4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"J5 — the real test: does FRA's DOUBLE gate (query-feat AND key-feat) make it more surgical\n2\tthan a content-addressed linear steer that must fire wherever the token appears?\n3\tAt MATCHED induction suppression, compare BROAD collateral:\n4\t  (A) per-position full-vocab KL on the induction sequence (off-target KL mass)\n5\t  (B) held-out real-text KL: install each content-addressed hook on normal English and measure\n6\t      how much it perturbs predictions where the cue token appears in NON-induction contexts.\n7\tFRA score-edit fires only where (query-feat[cue] & key-feat[prev-was-cue]) co-occur (induction-like);\n8\tActAdd-cue fires wherever current-token=cue -> corrupts the cue everywhere.\n9\t\"\"\"\n10\timport os, sys, json\n11\tsys.path.insert(0,\"/workspace/code\")\n12\timport torch, numpy as np\n13\timport matplotlib; matplotlib.use(\"Agg\"); import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n14\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n15\tfrom sae_lens import SAE\n16\tfrom fra.core.fra import _build_fra_result\n17\t\n18\tOUT=os.environ.get(\"OUTDIR\",\".\"); dev=\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n19\ttorch.set_grad_enabled(False)\n20\tmodel=HookedTransformer.from_pretrained(\"gpt2\",device=dev); model.eval()\n21\tIND_HEADS=[(5,5),(6,9),(5,1),(7,10),(7,2)]; LAYERS=sorted(set(L for L,H in IND_HEADS)); L0=min(LAYERS)\n22\t\n23\tdef kl_full(p_logits,q_logits):  # mean KL(p||q) over positions; [seq,vocab]\n24\t    lp=torch.log_softmax(p_logits.float(),-1); lq=torch.log_softmax(q_logits.float(),-1)\n25\t    return (lp.exp()*(lp-lq)).sum(-1)  # [seq]\n26\t\n27\t# ============ Part 1: induction sequence, per-position KL locality ============\n28\ttorch.manual_seed(0); N=24\n29\tR=(torch.randperm(40000)[:N]+1000).tolist()\n30\ttoks=[model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+R+R\n31\ttt=torch.tensor(toks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); seq=tt.shape[1]\n32\tedges=[(1+N+t,t+2) for t in range(N-1)]; ind_targets={1+N+t:R[t+1] for t in range(N-1)}\n33\tnames=[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]\n34\tclean_logits,cache=model.run_with_cache(tt,names_filter=lambda n:n in names)\n35\tclean_logits=clean_logits[0]\n36\tdef cp_at(lg,t): return torch.softmax(lg[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()\n37\tsaes={L:(SAE.from_pretrained(\"gpt2-small-res-jb\",f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\",device=dev)) for L in LAYERS}\n38\tsaes={L:(s[0] if isinstance(s,tuple) else s) for L,s in saes.items()}\n39\tHFRA={}\n40\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n41\t    sae=saes[L]; act=cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]\n42\t    feats=sae.encode(act).float(); x_hat=feats@sae.W_dec.float()+sae.b_dec.float()\n43\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,feats,sae.W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=x_hat,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n44\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n45\t    HFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n46\tresid={L:cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0] for L in LAYERS}\n47\tdef edge_pairs(LH,e,m):\n48\t    d=HFRA[LH]; loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==e[0])&(d[\"kk\"]==e[1]))[0]\n49\t    order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:m]]\n50\t    return set((int(d[\"ii\"][o]),int(d[\"jj\"][o])) for o in order)\n51\tdef pairs_delta(LH,pset):\n52\t    d=HFRA[LH]; out=np.zeros((seq,seq))\n53\t    sel=[(int(d[\"ii\"][n]),int(d[\"jj\"][n])) in pset for n in range(len(d[\"vv\"]))]\n54\t    for n in np.where(sel)[0]: out[d[\"qq\"][n],d[\"kk\"][n]]+=d[\"vv\"][n]\n55\t    return out\n56\tdef fra_run(t,c,M=12):\n57\t    deltas={LH:pairs_delta(LH,edge_pairs(LH,edges[t],M)) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n58\t    byL={}\n59\t    for LH,dd in deltas.items(): byL.setdefault(LH[0],{})[LH[1]]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*c\n60\t    hooks=[]\n61\t    for L,hd in byL.items():\n62\t        def mk(hd):\n63\t            def hook(s,hook):\n64\t                for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:seq,:seq]-=sd\n65\t                return s\n66\t            return hook\n67\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n68\t    return model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks)[0]\n69\tdef actadd_run(t,s):  # content-addressed: subtract cue r_t direction at BOTH its occurrences\n70\t    rt=R[t]; positions=[1+t,1+N+t]\n71\t    vX=resid[L0][1+N+t]-resid[L0].mean(0); vX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n72\t    def hook(act,hook):\n73\t        for p in positions: act[0,p,:]=act[0,p,:]-s*vX*act[0,p,:].norm()\n74\t        return act\n75\t    return model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",hook)])[0]\n76\t\n77\ttargets=[t for t in range(N-1) if cp_at(clean_logits,t)>0.85][:8]\n78\t# match suppression ~0.7: FRA c=8, ActAdd s search\n79\tfra_off=[]; aa_off=[]; fra_supp=[]; aa_supp=[]\n80\tfor t in targets:\n81\t    lf=fra_run(t,8); la=None\n82\t    # pick ActAdd s giving comparable suppression to FRA\n83\t    fs=1-torch.softmax(lf[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()/cp_at(clean_logits,t)\n84\t    best=None\n85\t    for s in [0.5,1,2,4]:\n86\t        l=actadd_run(t,s); sup=1-torch.softmax(l[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()/cp_at(clean_logits,t)\n87\t        if best is None or abs(sup-fs)<best[0]: best=(abs(sup-fs),l,sup)\n88\t    la=best[1]; as_=best[2]\n89\t    klf=kl_full(clean_logits,lf); kla=kl_full(clean_logits,la)\n90\t    qpos=edges[t][0]\n91\t    off_f=float(klf.sum().item()-klf[qpos].item())   # KL mass away from the target query position\n92\t    off_a=float(kla.sum().item()-kla[qpos].item())\n93\t    fra_off.append(off_f); aa_off.append(off_a); fra_supp.append(fs); aa_supp.append(as_)\n94\t    # count positions changed (KL>0.01)\n95\tprint(\"PART 1 — induction-sequence locality (matched suppression):\",flush=True)\n96\tprint(f\"  FRA   : suppression {np.mean(fra_supp):.2f}  off-target KL mass {np.mean(fra_off):.3f}\",flush=True)\n97\tprint(f\"  ActAdd: suppression {np.mean(aa_supp):.2f}  off-target KL mass {np.mean(aa_off):.3f}\",flush=True)\n98\tprint(f\"  ratio ActAdd/FRA off-target collateral: {np.mean(aa_off)/max(np.mean(fra_off),1e-4):.1f}x\",flush=True)\n99\t\n100\t# ============ Part 2: held-out real text, cue token in normal contexts ============\n101\treal=(\" The war lasted for many years. During the war, soldiers fought bravely. \"\n102\t      \"After the war ended, the war was remembered by all who lived through the war.\")\n103\trtoks=model.tokenizer.encode(real)\n104\t# cue = a token that appears >=3 times\n105\tfrom collections import Counter\n106\tcnt=Counter(rtoks); cue=max([tk for tk,c in cnt.items() if c>=3], key=lambda tk:cnt[tk])\n107\tcue_str=model.tokenizer.decode([cue])\n108\trt=torch.tensor([model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+rtoks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); rseq=rt.shape[1]\n109\tcue_pos=[i for i,tk in enumerate([model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+rtoks) if tk==cue]\n110\tprint(f\"\\nPART 2 — held-out real text. cue='{cue_str}' appears at {cue_pos}\",flush=True)\n111\trclean,rcache=model.run_with_cache(rt,names_filter=lambda n:n in\n112\t    [f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS])\n113\trclean=rclean[0]\n114\t# FRA content-addressed on real text: ablate cue's induction pairs (computed from the induction seq pair-set\n115\t# for a cue-matched edge is hard cross-context; instead: ablate the induction-head score wherever\n116\t# query token == cue AND key is the position after a previous cue occurrence -> emulate by recomputing FRA on real text\n117\trfeats={L:saes[L].encode(rcache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]).float() for L in LAYERS}\n118\tRFRA={}\n119\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n120\t    fe=rfeats[L]; xh=fe@saes[L].W_dec.float()+saes[L].b_dec.float()\n121\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,fe,saes[L].W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=xh,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n122\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n123\t    RFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n124\t# cue induction pairs on real text: query positions where token==cue, key = position right after a PRIOR cue\n125\tcue_edges=[]\n126\tfor qi in cue_pos:\n127\t    for ki in cue_pos:\n128\t        if ki+1<qi: cue_edges.append((qi,ki+1))  # attend back to token after an earlier cue\n129\t# build FRA delta on real text for these edges (top-M pairs each), apply with overdrive\n130\tdef real_fra_delta(c=8,M=12):\n131\t    byL={}\n132\t    for (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n133\t        d=RFRA[(L,H)]; dd=np.zeros((rseq,rseq))\n134\t        for (qi,ki) in cue_edges:\n135\t            loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==qi)&(d[\"kk\"]==ki))[0]\n136\t            order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:M]]\n137\t            for o in order: dd[qi,ki]+=d[\"vv\"][o]\n138\t        byL.setdefault(L,{})[H]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*c\n139\t    return byL\n140\tbyL=real_fra_delta()\n141\thooks=[]\n142\tfor L,hd in byL.items():\n143\t    def mk(hd):\n144\t        def hook(s,hook):\n145\t            for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:rseq,:rseq]-=sd\n146\t            return s\n147\t        return hook\n148\t    hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n149\tr_fra=model.run_with_hooks(rt,fwd_hooks=hooks)[0]\n150\t# ActAdd content-addressed on real text: subtract cue dir wherever token==cue\n151\tvX=rcache[f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\"][0][cue_pos[0]]-rcache[f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\"][0].mean(0)\n152\tvX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n153\tdef ahook(act,hook):\n154\t    for p in cue_pos: act[0,p,:]=act[0,p,:]-2.0*vX*act[0,p,:].norm()\n155\t    return act\n156\tr_aa=model.run_with_hooks(rt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",ahook)])[0]\n157\tklf=kl_full(rclean,r_fra); kla=kl_full(rclean,r_aa)\n158\tprint(f\"  FRA   : total real-text KL {klf.sum().item():.3f}  (mean/pos {klf.mean().item():.4f})\",flush=True)\n159\tprint(f\"  ActAdd: total real-text KL {kla.sum().item():.3f}  (mean/pos {kla.mean().item():.4f})\",flush=True)\n160\tprint(f\"  KL at cue positions: FRA {klf[cue_pos].mean().item():.4f}  ActAdd {kla[cue_pos].mean().item():.4f}\",flush=True)\n161\t\n162\tout={\"part1\":{\"fra_supp\":float(np.mean(fra_supp)),\"aa_supp\":float(np.mean(aa_supp)),\n163\t              \"fra_offtarget_kl\":float(np.mean(fra_off)),\"aa_offtarget_kl\":float(np.mean(aa_off)),\n164\t              \"ratio\":float(np.mean(aa_off)/max(np.mean(fra_off),1e-4))},\n165\t     \"part2\":{\"cue\":cue_str,\"fra_total_kl\":float(klf.sum().item()),\"aa_total_kl\":float(kla.sum().item()),\n166\t              \"fra_cue_kl\":float(klf[cue_pos].mean().item()),\"aa_cue_kl\":float(kla[cue_pos].mean().item())}}\n167\tjson.dump(out,open(os.path.join(OUT,\"j5.json\"),\"w\"),indent=2)\n168\tfig,ax=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(9,4))\n169\tax[0].bar([\"FRA-QK\",\"ActAdd-cue\"],[np.mean(fra_off),np.mean(aa_off)],color=['C0','C1'])\n170\tax[0].set_title(f\"off-target collateral on induction seq\\n(matched suppression ~{np.mean(fra_supp):.0%})\"); ax[0].set_ylabel(\"off-target KL mass (nats)\")\n171\tax[1].bar([\"FRA-QK\",\"ActAdd-cue\"],[klf.sum().item(),kla.sum().item()],color=['C0','C1'])\n172\tax[1].set_title(f\"held-out real-text collateral\\n(cue='{cue_str.strip()}')\"); ax[1].set_ylabel(\"total KL vs clean (nats)\")\n173\tplt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUT,\"j5_collateral.png\"),dpi=110)\n174\tprint(\"\\nDONE j5\",flush=True)\n175\t"}]},"uuid":"46435761-d3a1-4b5e-90a8-ce71c111e9b5","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:38.805Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e8e3711-5217-4918-92be-b066ad970b1f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"82107c11-28b5-4d18-b1c5-e47b73f2c888","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXEX5AqpVpVByASFcjx8QL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"J4 — core win: selectively suppress ONE token's induction copying.\n2\tMethods aim to drop target token X's copy-prob while sparing other tokens:\n3\t  FRA-QK selective : ablate X's induction feature-pairs across all induction heads (over-drive c, sweep)\n4\t  ActAdd-X(query)  : subtract s * v_X (token-X identity dir) at X's query position, before induction layers (sweep s)\n5\t  random-pair      : FRA machinery but RANDOM pairs (null: should NOT suppress target)  [sanity]\n6\t  position-oracle  : zero the target edge scores across heads (selective, needs positions)\n7\t  head-ablate-all  : mean-ablate all induction heads (non-selective ref: kills all copying)\n8\tCollateral = mean |Δcopyprob| on the OTHER induction tokens (within-task selectivity).\n9\tWin = FRA reaches high target suppression at low collateral on a Pareto where ActAdd cannot.\n10\t\"\"\"\n11\timport os, sys, json\n12\tsys.path.insert(0,\"/workspace/code\")\n13\timport torch, numpy as np\n14\timport matplotlib; matplotlib.use(\"Agg\"); import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n15\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n16\tfrom sae_lens import SAE\n17\tfrom fra.core.fra import _build_fra_result\n18\t\n19\tOUT=os.environ.get(\"OUTDIR\",\".\"); dev=\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n20\ttorch.set_grad_enabled(False)\n21\tmodel=HookedTransformer.from_pretrained(\"gpt2\",device=dev); model.eval()\n22\tIND_HEADS=[(5,5),(6,9),(5,1),(7,10),(7,2)]; LAYERS=sorted(set(L for L,H in IND_HEADS))\n23\tL0=min(LAYERS)\n24\ttorch.manual_seed(0); N=24\n25\tR=(torch.randperm(40000)[:N]+1000).tolist()\n26\ttoks=[model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+R+R\n27\ttt=torch.tensor(toks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); seq=tt.shape[1]\n28\tedges=[(1+N+t,t+2) for t in range(N-1)]; ind_targets={1+N+t:R[t+1] for t in range(N-1)}\n29\tnames=[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]\n30\tlogits,cache=model.run_with_cache(tt,names_filter=lambda n:n in names)\n31\tdef cpvec(lg):\n32\t    p=torch.softmax(lg[0].float(),-1); return np.array([p[q,ind_targets[q]].item() for q,k in edges])\n33\tbase=cpvec(logits)\n34\tsaes={L:(SAE.from_pretrained(\"gpt2-small-res-jb\",f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\",device=dev)) for L in LAYERS}\n35\tsaes={L:(s[0] if isinstance(s,tuple) else s) for L,s in saes.items()}\n36\tHFRA={}; rng=np.random.default_rng(0)\n37\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n38\t    sae=saes[L]; act=cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]\n39\t    feats=sae.encode(act).float(); x_hat=feats@sae.W_dec.float()+sae.b_dec.float()\n40\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,feats,sae.W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=x_hat,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n41\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n42\t    HFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n43\tSC={(L,H):cache[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\"][0,H].float().cpu().numpy() for (L,H) in IND_HEADS}\n44\tresid={L:cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0] for L in LAYERS}\n45\t\n46\tdef edge_pairs(LH,e,m):\n47\t    d=HFRA[LH]; loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==e[0])&(d[\"kk\"]==e[1]))[0]\n48\t    order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:m]]\n49\t    return set((int(d[\"ii\"][o]),int(d[\"jj\"][o])) for o in order)\n50\tdef pairs_delta(LH,pset):\n51\t    d=HFRA[LH]; out=np.zeros((seq,seq))\n52\t    sel=[(int(d[\"ii\"][n]),int(d[\"jj\"][n])) in pset for n in range(len(d[\"vv\"]))]\n53\t    for n in np.where(sel)[0]: out[d[\"qq\"][n],d[\"kk\"][n]]+=d[\"vv\"][n]\n54\t    return out\n55\tdef score_patch(deltas,scale):\n56\t    byL={}\n57\t    for (L,H),dd in deltas.items(): byL.setdefault(L,{})[H]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*scale\n58\t    hooks=[]\n59\t    for L,hd in byL.items():\n60\t        def mk(hd):\n61\t            def hook(s,hook):\n62\t                for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:seq,:seq]-=sd\n63\t                return s\n64\t            return hook\n65\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n66\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks))\n67\t\n68\tM=12\n69\ttargets=[t for t in range(N-1) if base[t]>0.8][:8]\n70\tbase_t=float(np.mean([base[t] for t in targets]))\n71\tdef collat(v,t): return float(np.mean([abs(v[s]-base[s]) for s in range(N-1) if s!=t]))\n72\tprint(f\"targets {targets} base_t {base_t:.3f}\",flush=True)\n73\t\n74\t# precompute per-target FRA deltas + random-pair deltas\n75\tfra_deltas={}; rnd_deltas={}\n76\tall_pairs={}\n77\tfor LH in IND_HEADS:\n78\t    d=HFRA[LH]; all_pairs[LH]=list(set(zip(d[\"ii\"].tolist(),d[\"jj\"].tolist())))\n79\tfor t in targets:\n80\t    e=edges[t]\n81\t    fra_deltas[t]={LH:pairs_delta(LH,edge_pairs(LH,e,M)) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n82\t    rnd_deltas[t]={LH:pairs_delta(LH,set(tuple(all_pairs[LH][i]) for i in rng.choice(len(all_pairs[LH]),M,replace=False))) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n83\t\n84\t# ActAdd-X: subtract s*vX at query pos (2nd-X) at resid_pre L0 (propagates to all induction heads)\n85\tdef actadd(t,s):\n86\t    qpos=edges[t][0]\n87\t    vX=resid[L0][qpos]-resid[L0].mean(0); vX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n88\t    def hook(act,hook):\n89\t        act[0,qpos,:]=act[0,qpos,:]-s*vX*act[0,qpos,:].norm()\n90\t        return act\n91\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",hook)]))\n92\t\n93\tCS=[1,2,4,8,16,32]; AS=[0.25,0.5,1,2,4,8]\n94\tdef curve(fn):  # returns list of (supp, collateral) over sweep\n95\t    pts=[]\n96\t    for x in (CS if fn=='fra' or fn=='rnd' else AS):\n97\t        tg=[]; co=[]\n98\t        for t in targets:\n99\t            if fn=='fra': v=score_patch(fra_deltas[t],x)\n100\t            elif fn=='rnd': v=score_patch(rnd_deltas[t],x)\n101\t            else: v=actadd(t,x)\n102\t            tg.append(v[t]); co.append(collat(v,t))\n103\t        pts.append((1-np.mean(tg)/base_t, float(np.mean(co)), x))\n104\t    return pts\n105\tfra_pts=curve('fra'); aa_pts=curve('aa'); rnd_pts=curve('rnd')\n106\tprint(\"\\nFRA (supp, collat, c):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in fra_pts],flush=True)\n107\tprint(\"ActAdd-X (supp, collat, s):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in aa_pts],flush=True)\n108\tprint(\"random-pair (supp, collat, c):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in rnd_pts],flush=True)\n109\t\n110\t# oracle + headablate single points\n111\tor_tg=[]; or_co=[]\n112\tfor t in targets:\n113\t    dd={LH:(np.zeros((seq,seq))) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n114\t    for LH in IND_HEADS: dd[LH][edges[t]]=SC[LH][edges[t][0],edges[t][1]]+20\n115\t    v=score_patch(dd,1.0); or_tg.append(v[t]); or_co.append(collat(v,t))\n116\tor_pt=(1-np.mean(or_tg)/base_t, float(np.mean(or_co)))\n117\tdef killall():\n118\t    hooks=[]\n119\t    for L in LAYERS:\n120\t        Hs=[H for (LL,H) in IND_HEADS if LL==L]\n121\t        def mk(Hs):\n122\t            def hook(z,hook):\n123\t                for H in Hs: z[0,:,H,:]=z[0,:,H,:].mean(0,keepdim=True)\n124\t                return z\n125\t            return hook\n126\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_z\",mk(Hs)))\n127\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks))\n128\tka=killall(); ka_pt=(1-np.mean([ka[t] for t in targets])/base_t, float(np.mean([collat(ka,t) for t in targets])))\n129\tprint(f\"oracle (supp,collat): {or_pt}\",flush=True)\n130\tprint(f\"head-ablate-all (supp,collat): {ka_pt}\",flush=True)\n131\t\n132\tout={\"base_t\":base_t,\"fra\":fra_pts,\"actadd\":aa_pts,\"random\":rnd_pts,\"oracle\":or_pt,\"headablate\":ka_pt}\n133\tjson.dump(out,open(os.path.join(OUT,\"j4.json\"),\"w\"),indent=2)\n134\tplt.figure(figsize=(6,4.5))\n135\tfor pts,lab,mk in [(fra_pts,\"FRA-QK selective\",\"o-\"),(aa_pts,\"ActAdd-X (linear)\",\"s-\"),(rnd_pts,\"random pairs (null)\",\"^:\")]:\n136\t    xs=[p[0] for p in pts]; ys=[p[1] for p in pts]; plt.plot(xs,ys,mk,label=lab)\n137\tplt.scatter([or_pt[0]],[or_pt[1]],c='green',marker='*',s=140,label=\"position oracle\")\n138\tplt.scatter([ka_pt[0]],[ka_pt[1]],c='red',marker='x',s=90,label=\"kill all heads (non-selective)\")\n139\tplt.xlabel(\"target-token copy suppression  (1 - cp/base)  → better\"); plt.ylabel(\"collateral |Δcp| on other tokens  ←better\")\n140\tplt.title(\"Selective induction suppression — FRA-QK vs baselines\\n(down-right = selective + strong)\")\n141\tplt.legend(fontsize=8); plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUT,\"j4_pareto.png\"),dpi=110)\n142\tprint(\"\\nDONE j4\",flush=True)\n143\t"}]},"uuid":"1f152e47-8a6d-4138-abd9-0b05902029ef","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:53.599Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82107c11-28b5-4d18-b1c5-e47b73f2c888","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"bccae08a-f0e7-4796-9582-913390eab9ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgAz8mDEtYSkQs2H1aNpkg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"\n2\tFeature-Resolved Attention (FRA) computation.\n3\t\n4\tProvides two entry points for computing 4-D FRA tensors:\n5\t  - ``get_sentence_fra_batch``: single-model SAE path\n6\t  - ``get_sentence_fra_crosscoder``: two-model crosscoder path\n7\t\n8\tBoth share the core tensor construction via ``_build_fra_result()``.\n9\t\"\"\"\n10\t\n11\timport math\n12\t\n13\timport numpy as np\n14\timport torch\n15\tfrom typing import Any, Dict\n16\tfrom einops import einsum\n17\tfrom tqdm import tqdm\n18\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n19\t\n20\tfrom fra.core.activations import get_llm_activations\n21\tfrom fra.core.helpers import get_W_K, apply_rope_to_projected, _extract_rope_params\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t# ── Top-k sparsification ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tdef topk_sparsify(\n28\t    feature_activations: torch.Tensor,\n29\t    top_k: int | None,\n30\t) -> torch.Tensor:\n31\t    \"\"\"Keep only top-k features per position by absolute activation magnitude.\n32\t\n33\t    Args:\n34\t        feature_activations: [seq_len, d_sae] tensor of feature activations.\n35\t        top_k: Number of features to keep per position.  None keeps all\n36\t               active (non-zero) features without truncation.\n37\t\n38\t    Returns:\n39\t        [seq_len, d_sae] tensor with at most top_k non-zero entries per row.\n40\t    \"\"\"\n41\t    if top_k is None:\n42\t        return feature_activations\n43\t\n44\t    seq_len = feature_activations.shape[0]\n45\t    topk_features = []\n46\t    for pos in range(seq_len):\n47\t        feat = feature_activations[pos]\n48\t        n_active = (feat != 0).sum().item()\n49\t\n50\t        if n_active > 0:\n51\t            k = min(top_k, n_active)\n52\t            _, topk_idx = torch.topk(feat.abs(), k)\n53\t            sparse_feat = torch.zeros_like(feat)\n54\t            sparse_feat[topk_idx] = feat[topk_idx]\n55\t        else:\n56\t            sparse_feat = torch.zeros_like(feat)\n57\t\n58\t        topk_features.append(sparse_feat)\n59\t\n60\t    return torch.stack(topk_features)\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t# ── Core FRA loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64\t\n65\t\n66\tdef compute_fra_sparse(\n67\t    topk_features: torch.Tensor,\n68\t    W_dec: torch.Tensor,\n69\t    W_Q: torch.Tensor,\n70\t    W_K: torch.Tensor,\n71\t    attn_scale: float,\n72\t    *,\n73\t    rms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n74\t    dec_norms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n75\t    rope_sin: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n76\t    rope_cos: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n77\t    rotary_dim: int | None = None,\n78\t    rotary_adjacent_pairs: bool = False,\n79\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n80\t    verbose: bool = False,\n81\t    layer_head_label: str = \"\",\n82\t) -> torch.sparse_coo_tensor:\n83\t    \"\"\"Compute the 4-D FRA sparse tensor from pre-computed feature activations.\n84\t\n85\t    All model-specific setup (activation extraction, encoding, weight lookup)\n86\t    happens in the caller; this function is the shared inner loop.\n87\t\n88\t    Args:\n89\t        topk_features: ``[seq_len, d_sae]`` already top-k sparsified.\n90\t        W_dec:  ``[d_sae, d_model]`` decoder weight matrix.\n91\t        W_Q:    ``[d_model, d_head]`` query projection for one head.\n92\t        W_K:    ``[d_model, d_head]`` key projection for one head.\n93\t        attn_scale: ``sqrt(d_head)`` scaling factor.\n94\t        rms:    Optional ``[seq_len]`` per-position RMS values for RMSNorm\n95\t                correction.  When provided, each interaction is divided by\n96\t                ``rms[query_idx] * rms[key_idx]``.\n97\t        dec_norms: Optional ``[d_sae]`` decoder-weight norms for SAEs\n98\t                trained with ``rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm=True``.\n99\t        rope_sin: Optional ``[n_ctx, rotary_dim]`` precomputed sine table\n100\t                from the attention block.  Pass for RoPE models (Gemma, Llama).\n101\t        rope_cos: Optional ``[n_ctx, rotary_dim]`` precomputed cosine table.\n102\t        rotary_dim: Number of RoPE dimensions (``model.cfg.rotary_dim``).\n103\t        rotary_adjacent_pairs: RoPE pair ordering flag from model config.\n104\t        chunk_size: Number of query positions per GPU batch before flushing\n105\t                to CPU.  Controls peak GPU memory.\n106\t        verbose: Show progress bar.\n107\t        layer_head_label: Label for progress bar (e.g. ``\"L5H3\"``).\n108\t\n109\t    Returns:\n110\t        ``torch.sparse_coo_tensor`` on CPU, shape\n111\t        ``[seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae]``, coalesced.\n112\t    \"\"\"\n113\t    seq_len = topk_features.shape[0]\n114\t    d_sae = topk_features.shape[1]\n115\t    shape = (seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae)\n116\t\n117\t    all_indices_cpu: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n118\t    all_values_cpu: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n119\t\n120\t    total_pairs = seq_len * (seq_len + 1) // 2\n121\t    pbar = tqdm(\n122\t        total=total_pairs,\n123\t        desc=f\"Computing FRA ({layer_head_label})\" if layer_head_label else \"Computing FRA\",\n124\t        disable=not verbose,\n125\t    )\n126\t\n127\t    for q_start in range(0, seq_len, chunk_size):\n128\t        q_end = min(q_start + chunk_size, seq_len)\n129\t        chunk_indices: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n130\t        chunk_values: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n131\t\n132\t        for query_idx in range(q_start, q_end):\n133\t            q_feat = topk_features[query_idx]\n134\t            q_active = torch.where(q_feat != 0)[0]\n135\t\n136\t            if len(q_active) == 0:\n137\t                pbar.update(query_idx + 1)\n138\t                continue\n139\t\n140\t            q_vecs = W_dec[q_active]                          # [n_q, d_model]\n141\t            q_proj = q_vecs @ W_Q                             # [n_q, d_head]\n142\t            q_scales = q_feat[q_active]                       # [n_q]\n143\t            if dec_norms is not None:\n144\t                q_scales = q_scales / dec_norms[q_active]\n145\t\n146\t            # Apply RoPE to query once per query position (outside key loop)\n147\t            if rope_sin is not None:\n148\t                q_proj = apply_rope_to_projected(\n149\t                    q_proj, query_idx, rope_sin, rope_cos,\n150\t                    rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n151\t                )\n152\t\n153\t            for key_idx in range(query_idx + 1):\n154\t                k_feat = topk_features[key_idx]\n155\t                k_active = torch.where(k_feat != 0)[0]\n156\t\n157\t                if len(k_active) == 0:\n158\t                    pbar.update(1)\n159\t                    continue\n160\t\n161\t                k_vecs = W_dec[k_active]                      # [n_k, d_model]\n162\t                k_proj = k_vecs @ W_K                         # [n_k, d_head]\n163\t\n164\t                # Apply RoPE to key for this key position\n165\t                if rope_sin is not None:\n166\t                    k_proj = apply_rope_to_projected(\n167\t                        k_proj, key_idx, rope_sin, rope_cos,\n168\t                        rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n169\t                    )\n170\t                k_scales = k_feat[k_active]                   # [n_k]\n171\t                if dec_norms is not None:\n172\t                    k_scales = k_scales / dec_norms[k_active]\n173\t\n174\t                int_matrix = (q_proj @ k_proj.T) / attn_scale  # [n_q, n_k]\n175\t                int_matrix = int_matrix * q_scales.unsqueeze(1) * k_scales.unsqueeze(0)\n176\t\n177\t                if rms is not None:\n178\t                    int_matrix = int_matrix / (rms[query_idx] * rms[key_idx])\n179\t\n180\t                mask = int_matrix.abs() > 1e-10\n181\t                if mask.any():\n182\t                    local_r, local_c = torch.where(mask)\n183\t                    n_int = len(local_r)\n184\t\n185\t                    pos_indices = torch.empty((4, n_int), dtype=torch.long)\n186\t                    pos_indices[0] = query_idx\n187\t                    pos_indices[1] = key_idx\n188\t                    pos_indices[2] = q_active[local_r].cpu()\n189\t                    pos_indices[3] = k_active[local_c].cpu()\n190\t\n191\t                    chunk_indices.append(pos_indices)\n192\t                    chunk_values.append(int_matrix[mask].detach().cpu().float())\n193\t\n194\t                pbar.update(1)\n195\t\n196\t        all_indices_cpu.extend(chunk_indices)\n197\t        all_values_cpu.extend(chunk_values)\n198\t\n199\t        device = topk_features.device\n200\t        if device.type != \"cpu\":\n201\t            torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n202\t\n203\t    pbar.close()\n204\t\n205\t    if all_indices_cpu:\n206\t        indices = torch.cat(all_indices_cpu, dim=1)\n207\t        values = torch.cat(all_values_cpu)\n208\t        fra_sparse = torch.sparse_coo_tensor(\n209\t            indices, values, size=shape, device=\"cpu\", dtype=torch.float32,\n210\t        ).coalesce()\n211\t    else:\n212\t        fra_sparse = torch.sparse_coo_tensor(\n213\t            torch.zeros((4, 0), dtype=torch.long),\n214\t            torch.zeros(0, dtype=torch.float32),\n215\t            size=shape, device=\"cpu\",\n216\t        )\n217\t\n218\t    return fra_sparse\n219\t\n220\t\n221\tdef _build_fra_result(\n222\t    model: HookedTransformer,\n223\t    layer: int,\n224\t    head: int,\n225\t    feature_activations: torch.Tensor,\n226\t    W_dec: torch.Tensor,\n227\t    device,\n228\t    *,\n229\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n230\t    rms_activations: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n231\t    dec_norms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n232\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n233\t    verbose: bool = False,\n234\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n235\t    \"\"\"Shared post-encoding FRA construction.\n236\t\n237\t    Handles top-k sparsification, weight extraction, RMSNorm correction,\n238\t    RoPE, ``compute_fra_sparse``, device transfer, and result assembly.\n239\t\n240\t    Args:\n241\t        model: Target model (for W_Q / W_K and RoPE parameters).\n242\t        layer: Attention layer index.\n243\t        head: Attention head index.\n244\t        feature_activations: ``[seq, d_sae]`` raw encoded features.\n245\t        W_dec: ``[d_sae, d_model]`` decoder weights.\n246\t        device: Torch device for the result tensor.\n247\t        top_k: Features per position to keep (None = all).\n248\t        rms_activations: ``[seq, d_model]`` residual stream for RMSNorm\n249\t            correction, or None to skip.\n250\t        dec_norms: ``[d_sae]`` decoder norms for rescale correction, or None.\n251\t        chunk_size: GPU batch size for ``compute_fra_sparse``.\n252\t        verbose: Show progress.\n253\t\n254\t    Returns:\n255\t        Dict with ``fra_tensor_sparse``, ``shape``, ``seq_len``,\n256\t        ``total_interactions``, ``feature_activations``, ``topk_features``.\n257\t    \"\"\"\n258\t    topk_features = topk_sparsify(feature_activations, top_k).float()\n259\t\n260\t    # Attention weights — float32 for accumulation precision\n261\t    W_Q = model.blocks[layer].attn.W_Q[head].float()       # [d_model, d_head]\n262\t    W_K_mat = get_W_K(model, layer, head).float()           # [d_model, d_head]\n263\t    d_head = W_Q.shape[-1]\n264\t    attn_scale = math.sqrt(d_head)\n265\t\n266\t    # RMSNorm correction\n267\t    rms = None\n268\t    if rms_activations is not None:\n269\t        eps = model.cfg.eps\n270\t        rms = (rms_activations.float().pow(2).mean(dim=-1) + eps).sqrt()\n271\t\n272\t    # RoPE\n273\t    rope_sin, rope_cos, rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs = (\n274\t        _extract_rope_params(model, layer)\n275\t    )\n276\t\n277\t    fra_tensor_sparse = compute_fra_sparse(\n278\t        topk_features, W_dec.float(), W_Q, W_K_mat, attn_scale,\n279\t        rms=rms,\n280\t        dec_norms=dec_norms,\n281\t        rope_sin=rope_sin,\n282\t        rope_cos=rope_cos,\n283\t        rotary_dim=rotary_dim,\n284\t        rotary_adjacent_pairs=rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n285\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n286\t        verbose=verbose,\n287\t        layer_head_label=f\"L{layer}H{head}\",\n288\t    )\n289\t\n290\t    # Move to device if it fits\n291\t    if str(device) != \"cpu\":\n292\t        try:\n293\t            fra_tensor_sparse = fra_tensor_sparse.to(device)\n294\t        except RuntimeError:\n295\t            if verbose:\n296\t                print(\"Warning: sparse tensor too large for GPU, keeping on CPU.\")\n297\t\n298\t    seq_len = feature_activations.shape[0]\n299\t    d_sae = feature_activations.shape[-1]\n300\t    total_interactions = fra_tensor_sparse._nnz()\n301\t    shape = fra_tensor_sparse.shape\n302\t\n303\t    if verbose:\n304\t        _k = top_k if top_k is not None else d_sae\n305\t        density = total_interactions / max(seq_len * seq_len * _k * _k, 1)\n306\t        print(\n307\t            f\"4D FRA tensor: shape={shape}, \"\n308\t            f\"nnz={total_interactions:,}, density={density:.2%}\"\n309\t        )\n310\t\n311\t    return {\n312\t        \"fra_tensor_sparse\": fra_tensor_sparse,\n313\t        \"shape\": shape,\n314\t        \"seq_len\": seq_len,\n315\t        \"total_interactions\": total_interactions,\n316\t        \"feature_activations\": feature_activations,\n317\t        \"topk_features\": topk_features,\n318\t    }\n319\t\n320\t\n321\t# ── Legacy analysis helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────\n322\t\n323\t\n324\tdef lower_triangular_mask(pattern: np.ndarray) -> np.ma.MaskedArray:\n325\t    \"\"\"Apply lower triangular mask to attention pattern.\"\"\"\n326\t    mask = np.triu(np.ones(pattern.shape), k=1)\n327\t    return np.ma.array(np.tril(pattern, k=0), mask=mask)\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tdef attention_pattern_QK(llm: Any, layer: int, head: int, q_input: torch.Tensor,\n331\t                        q_do_bias: bool, k_input: torch.Tensor, k_do_bias: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n332\t    \"\"\"\n333\t    Compute attention pattern from query and key inputs.\n334\t\n335\t    Args:\n336\t        layer: Layer index\n337\t        head: Head index\n338\t        q_input: Query input tensor\n339\t        q_do_bias: Whether to add query bias\n340\t        k_input: Key input tensor\n341\t        k_do_bias: Whether to add key bias\n342\t\n343\t    Returns:\n344\t        Attention scores as numpy array\n345\t    \"\"\"\n346\t    W_Q = llm.blocks[layer].attn.W_Q[head]\n347\t    b_Q = llm.blocks[layer].attn.b_Q[head]\n348\t    W_K = llm.blocks[layer].attn.W_K[head]\n349\t    b_K = llm.blocks[layer].attn.b_K[head]\n350\t\n351\t    q = einsum(W_Q, q_input, \"d a, s d -> s a\")\n352\t    if q_do_bias:\n353\t        q += b_Q\n354\t\n355\t    k = einsum(W_K, k_input, \"d a, s d -> s a\")\n356\t    if k_do_bias:\n357\t        k += b_K\n358\t\n359\t    d_head = W_Q.shape[-1]\n360\t    attention_scores = einsum(q, k, \"q a, k a -> q k\") / math.sqrt(d_head)\n361\t\n362\t    return attention_scores.detach().cpu().numpy()\n363\t\n364\t\n365\tdef analyze_feature_attention_interactions(model: Any, sae: Any, layer: int, head: int,\n366\t                                           input_text: str, query_position: int, key_position: int,\n367\t                                           hook_point: str = \"hook_attn_out\") -> Dict:\n368\t    \"\"\"\n369\t    Analyze interactions between features in attention.\n370\t\n371\t    Args:\n372\t        layer: Layer index\n373\t        head: Head index\n374\t        input_text: Input text to analyze\n375\t        query_position: Query position\n376\t        key_position: Key position\n377\t    \"\"\"\n378\t    activations_SD = get_llm_activations(model,input_text,hook_point=hook_point,layers=layer)\n379\t    feature_activations_SH = sae.encode(activations_SD)\n380\t\n381\t    feature_activations_query = feature_activations_SH[query_position]\n382\t    query_active_features = torch.where(feature_activations_query != 0)[0]\n383\t\n384\t    feature_activations_key = feature_activations_SH[key_position]\n385\t    key_active_features = torch.where(feature_activations_key != 0)[0]\n386\t\n387\t    query_activations_for_features = sae.W_dec[query_active_features]\n388\t    key_activations_for_features = sae.W_dec[key_active_features]\n389\t\n390\t    interaction_matrix_unscaled = attention_pattern_QK(model, layer, head,\n391\t                                                        query_activations_for_features, False,\n392\t                                                        key_activations_for_features, False)\n393\t\n394\t\n395\t\n396\t    # Convert to numpy after using for indexing\n397\t    query_features_tensor = query_active_features\n398\t    key_features_tensor = key_active_features\n399\t\n400\t    matrix_scaling = feature_activations_query[query_features_tensor].unsqueeze(1) * \\\n401\t                    feature_activations_key[key_features_tensor].unsqueeze(0)\n402\t    matrix_scaling = matrix_scaling.detach().cpu().numpy()\n403\t\n404\t    query_active_features = query_features_tensor.cpu().numpy()\n405\t    key_active_features = key_features_tensor.cpu().numpy()\n406\t\n407\t    return {\n408\t        'query_active_features': query_active_features,\n409\t        'key_active_features': key_active_features,\n410\t        'interaction_matrix_unscaled': interaction_matrix_unscaled,\n411\t        'matrix_scaling': matrix_scaling,\n412\t        'interaction_matrix': interaction_matrix_unscaled * matrix_scaling\n413\t    }\n414\t\n415\t\n416\tdef get_sentence_averages(llm:Any,sae:Any,layer:int,head:int,input_text:str,hook_point:str=\"attn.hook_z\"):\n417\t\ttext_length=128\n418\t\thidden_dim=sae.d_sae\n419\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n420\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n421\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n422\t\tcount=0\n423\t\tfor key_index in tqdm(range(text_length), disable=True):\n424\t\t\tfor query_index in range(key_index,text_length):\n425\t\t\t\t\tfeature_analysis=analyze_feature_attention_interactions(llm,sae,layer,head,input_text,query_index,key_index,hook_point)\n426\t\t\t\t\tint_matrix=feature_analysis[\"interaction_matrix\"]\n427\t\t\t\t\tquery_active_features=feature_analysis[\"query_active_features\"]\n428\t\t\t\t\tkey_active_features=feature_analysis[\"key_active_features\"]\n429\t\t\t\t\tdata_independent=feature_analysis[\"interaction_matrix_unscaled\"]\n430\t\n431\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_int=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n432\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_int[query_active_features[:,None],key_active_features[None,:]]=int_matrix\n433\t\n434\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_localization=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n435\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_localization[query_active_features[:,None],key_active_features[None,:]]=np.abs(int_matrix)*(query_index-key_index)\n436\t\n437\t\n438\t\n439\t\n440\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix=data_dep_int_matrix+resized_data_dependent_int\n441\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs=data_dep_int_matrix_abs+np.abs(resized_data_dependent_int)\n442\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=data_dep_localization_matrix+resized_data_dependent_localization\n443\t\n444\t\t\t\t\tcount+=1\n445\t\n446\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix/=count\n447\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=data_dep_localization_matrix/np.clip(data_dep_int_matrix_abs,a_min=1,a_max=None)\n448\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs/=count\n449\t\n450\t\treturn data_dep_int_matrix,data_dep_int_matrix_abs,data_dep_localization_matrix\n451\t\n452\t\n453\t\n454\t\n455\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n456\t# Entry point: single-model SAE path\n457\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n458\t\n459\t\n460\t@torch.no_grad()\n461\tdef get_sentence_fra_batch(\n462\t    model: HookedTransformer,\n463\t    sae: Any,\n464\t    text: str,\n465\t    layer: int,\n466\t    head: int,\n467\t    max_length: int = 128,\n468\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n469\t    verbose: bool = False,\n470\t    hook_point: str = \"ln1.hook_normalized\",\n471\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n472\t    normalize_by_decoder_norm: bool | None = None,\n473\t    prepend_bos: bool | None = None,\n474\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n475\t    \"\"\"\n476\t    Compute full 4D Feature-Resolved Attention tensor for a sentence.\n477\t    Returns a sparse representation to avoid memory issues.\n478\t\n479\t    hook_point controls which activation the SAE was trained on:\n480\t      - \"ln1.hook_normalized\"  (default, correct for FRA): decoder vectors live in\n481\t        the same d_model space that W_Q / W_K project from.  This is the only\n482\t        mathematically correct choice.\n483\t      - \"attn.hook_z\"          (legacy, for pre-trained hook_z SAEs): decoder\n484\t        vectors are in concatenated-heads space, not d_model space; the QK\n485\t        attention score computation is therefore approximate.\n486\t\n487\t    Args:\n488\t        model: The transformer model\n489\t        sae: The SAE (any object with .encode() and .W_dec attributes)\n490\t        text: Input text to analyze\n491\t        layer: Which layer to analyze\n492\t        head: Which attention head to analyze\n493\t        max_length: Maximum sequence length\n494\t        top_k: Number of top features to keep per position\n495\t        verbose: Whether to show progress\n496\t        hook_point: Hookpoint the SAE was trained on (relative to blocks.{layer}.)\n497\t        chunk_size: Number of query positions to process per GPU batch before\n498\t                    flushing results to CPU.  Reduce for large SAEs (e.g. Gemma-Scope)\n499\t                    to avoid GPU OOM.  Set to seq_len to process everything at once.\n500\t        normalize_by_decoder_norm: Whether to divide feature activations by\n501\t                    decoder weight norms to match SAEs trained with\n502\t                    rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm=True.  None (default) auto-detects\n503\t                    from the SAE config.  True/False forces the behaviour.\n504\t        prepend_bos: Whether to include special tokens (BOS) in tokenization.\n505\t                    None (default) uses the tokenizer's default behaviour.\n506\t                    True/False forces add_special_tokens on/off.\n507\t\n508\t    Returns:\n509\t        Dictionary containing:\n510\t            - fra_tensor_sparse: Sparse 4D tensor indices and values\n511\t            - shape: Shape of the full tensor [seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae]\n512\t            - seq_len: Actual sequence length\n513\t            - total_interactions: Total number of non-zero interactions\n514\t            - normalized: Whether decoder-norm normalization was applied\n515\t    \"\"\"\n516\t    device = next(model.parameters()).device\n517\t\n518\t    # Tokenise and truncate\n519\t    if prepend_bos is not None:\n520\t        tokens = model.tokenizer.encode(text, add_special_tokens=prepend_bos)\n521\t    else:\n522\t        tokens = model.tokenizer.encode(text)\n523\t    if max_length is not None and len(tokens) > max_length:\n524\t        tokens = tokens[:max_length]\n525\t\n526\t    tokens_tensor = torch.tensor(tokens).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n527\t    hook_name = f\"blocks.{layer}.{hook_point}\"\n528\t    _, cache = model.run_with_cache(tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name])\n529\t\n530\t    act = cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)  # remove batch dim\n531\t\n532\t    # hook_z is [seq_len, n_heads, d_head] → flatten to [seq_len, n_heads*d_head]\n533\t    # ln1.hook_normalized is already [seq_len, d_model]\n534\t    if act.dim() == 3:\n535\t        act = act.flatten(-2, -1)\n536\t\n537\t    # Encode to SAE features\n538\t    if verbose:\n539\t        print(f\"Encoding {act.shape[0]} positions to SAE features...\")\n540\t\n541\t    if hasattr(sae, 'encode'):\n542\t        feature_activations = sae.encode(act)   # [seq_len, d_sae]\n543\t    else:\n544\t        feature_activations = sae.sae.encode(act)\n545\t\n546\t    # If the SAE normalizes inputs (e.g. Gemma-Scope), the feature activations\n547\t    # are in the normalized scale.  Divide by the norm coefficient so that\n548\t    # FRA[q,k,i,j] sums to the actual (un-normalized) QK attention score.\n549\t    # Top-k ranking is unaffected (same scalar per position).\n550\t    if hasattr(sae, '_norm_coeff') and sae._norm_coeff is not None:\n551\t        feature_activations = feature_activations / sae._norm_coeff\n552\t\n553\t    # Get decoder weights\n554\t    if hasattr(sae, 'W_dec'):\n555\t        W_dec = sae.W_dec   # [d_sae, d_model]\n556\t    else:\n557\t        W_dec = sae.sae.W_dec\n558\t\n559\t    # Handle rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm: when the SAE was trained with this\n560\t    # flag, encode() returns activations scaled UP by ||W_dec[i]||, and decode()\n561\t    # scales them back DOWN.  The true per-feature contribution to x is\n562\t    #   (f[i] / ||W_dec[i]||) * W_dec[i]\n563\t    # but without correction FRA would use f[i] * W_dec[i], inflating each\n564\t    # entry by ||W_dec[q_feat]|| * ||W_dec[k_feat]||.\n565\t    if normalize_by_decoder_norm is None:\n566\t        inner = sae.sae if hasattr(sae, 'sae') else sae\n567\t        cfg = getattr(inner, 'cfg', None)\n568\t        do_normalize = getattr(cfg, 'rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm', False) if cfg else False\n569\t    else:\n570\t        do_normalize = normalize_by_decoder_norm\n571\t\n572\t    if do_normalize:\n573\t        dec_norms = W_dec.norm(dim=-1)  # [d_sae]\n574\t        if verbose:\n575\t            print(\"Applying decoder-norm correction (rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm)\")\n576\t    else:\n577\t        dec_norms = None\n578\t\n579\t    # RMSNorm correction is needed when the SAE's decoder vectors live in\n580\t    # residual-stream space but W_Q / W_K project from post-RMSNorm space.\n581\t    # Use the full reconstructed activations (not actual model activations)\n582\t    # so that FRA scores match coder-patched scores when all features are kept.\n583\t    if \"resid\" in hook_point:\n584\t        b_dec = sae.b_dec\n585\t        x_hat = feature_activations @ W_dec + b_dec\n586\t        rms_activations = x_hat\n587\t    else:\n588\t        rms_activations = None\n589\t\n590\t    result = _build_fra_result(\n591\t        model, layer, head, feature_activations, W_dec, device,\n592\t        top_k=top_k,\n593\t        rms_activations=rms_activations,\n594\t        dec_norms=dec_norms,\n595\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n596\t        verbose=verbose,\n597\t    )\n598\t    result[\"normalized\"] = do_normalize\n599\t    return result\n600\t\n601\t\n602\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n603\t# Entry point: two-model crosscoder path\n604\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n605\t\n606\t\n607\t@torch.no_grad()\n608\tdef get_sentence_fra_crosscoder(\n609\t    base_model: HookedTransformer,\n610\t    it_model: HookedTransformer,\n611\t    crosscoder: Any,\n612\t    tokens: list,\n613\t    head: int = 0,\n614\t    crosscoder_layer: int = 13,\n615\t    max_length: int = 128,\n616\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n617\t    verbose: bool = False,\n618\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n619\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n620\t    \"\"\"Compute 4-D FRA tensor using a model-diffing crosscoder.\n621\t\n622\t    The crosscoder was trained on ``hook_resid_post`` at ``crosscoder_layer``.\n623\t    That residual stream state is the input to the *next* layer's attention\n624\t    (``hook_resid_pre`` at ``crosscoder_layer + 1``), so we always analyse\n625\t    attention at ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.  The same activations are used\n626\t    for crosscoder encoding and for the RMSNorm correction.\n627\t\n628\t    The attention layer is **not** independently configurable — it is always\n629\t    ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.  This ensures the FRA decomposition corresponds\n630\t    to the features the crosscoder actually learned.\n631\t\n632\t    Args:\n633\t        base_model:  HookedTransformer for model-index 0 (base).\n634\t        it_model:    HookedTransformer for model-index 1 (instruct).\n635\t        crosscoder:  ``GemmaCrosscoderFRA`` instance.\n636\t        tokens:      Token IDs to analyse.  Caller is responsible for\n637\t                     tokenization (including chat template if needed).\n638\t        head:        Attention head index.\n639\t        crosscoder_layer:\n640\t            Layer from which to extract residual-stream activations for the\n641\t            crosscoder (default 13, matching the published checkpoint).\n642\t            Uses ``hook_resid_post`` at this layer.  The attention layer\n643\t            is derived as ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.\n644\t        max_length:  Maximum sequence length.\n645\t        top_k:       Keep only top-k features per position.\n646\t        verbose:     Show progress bar.\n647\t        chunk_size:  Query positions per GPU batch (controls peak memory).\n648\t\n649\t    Returns:\n650\t        Dict with keys:\n651\t          - ``fra_tensor_sparse``  (torch.sparse_coo_tensor, 4-D)\n652\t          - ``shape``\n653\t          - ``seq_len``\n654\t          - ``total_interactions``\n655\t          - ``feature_activations``  (torch.Tensor, [seq, d_sae])\n656\t          - ``topk_features``  (torch.Tensor, [seq, d_sae])\n657\t    \"\"\"\n658\t    layer = crosscoder_layer + 1\n659\t    target_model = base_model if crosscoder.model_idx == 0 else it_model\n660\t    other_model = it_model if crosscoder.model_idx == 0 else base_model\n661\t    device = next(target_model.parameters()).device\n662\t\n663\t    # Truncate if needed\n664\t    if max_length is not None and len(tokens) > max_length:\n665\t        tokens = tokens[:max_length]\n666\t    tokens_tensor = torch.tensor(tokens).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n667\t\n668\t    # Extract activations from both models at crosscoder_layer\n669\t    hook_name = f\"blocks.{crosscoder_layer}.hook_resid_post\"\n670\t\n671\t    _, target_cache = target_model.run_with_cache(\n672\t        tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name],\n673\t    )\n674\t    _, other_cache = other_model.run_with_cache(\n675\t        tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name],\n676\t    )\n677\t\n678\t    target_act = target_cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)      # [seq, d_model]\n679\t    other_act = other_cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)\n680\t\n681\t    # Stack in crosscoder order: [base, instruct]\n682\t    if crosscoder.model_idx == 0:\n683\t        x_stacked = torch.stack([target_act, other_act], dim=1)\n684\t    else:\n685\t        x_stacked = torch.stack([other_act, target_act], dim=1)\n686\t\n687\t    # Encode through crosscoder\n688\t    if verbose:\n689\t        print(f\"Encoding {target_act.shape[0]} positions through crosscoder...\")\n690\t    feature_activations = crosscoder.encode(x_stacked)   # [seq, d_sae]\n691\t\n692\t    # Crosscoder decoder vectors live in residual-stream space, so RMSNorm\n693\t    # correction is always needed.  Use the full reconstructed activations\n694\t    # (not actual model activations) so that FRA scores match coder-patched\n695\t    # scores when all features are kept.\n696\t    #\n697\t    # Decode in float32 to match the precision used for per-feature W_dec\n698\t    # projections inside compute_fra_sparse (which casts W_dec.float()).\n699\t    # Using the native float16 decode would introduce precision mismatch\n700\t    # between the RMS denominator and the per-feature numerators.\n701\t    b_dec_rms = crosscoder.b_dec.float().to(device)\n702\t    x_hat = feature_activations.float() @ crosscoder.W_dec.float() + b_dec_rms\n703\t    return _build_fra_result(\n704\t        target_model, layer, head, feature_activations, crosscoder.W_dec, device,\n705\t        top_k=top_k,\n706\t        rms_activations=x_hat,\n707\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n708\t        verbose=verbose,\n709\t    )\n710\t\n711\t\n712\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n713\t    print('main character')\n714\t"}]},"uuid":"19213172-731a-4b2c-aa79-194f29b14464","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:58.255Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bccae08a-f0e7-4796-9582-913390eab9ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"cc86164e-6b44-47d4-b1f2-557cc4b2d021","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a0186935e26cce807","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JhkJrLQNj7AQmBKQE3ty45","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"J1 — induction-head FRA exploration on GPT-2 small.\n2\tGoals: (1) pick the strongest induction head; (2) validate that the FRA decomposition\n3\treconstructs the real pre-softmax attention scores; (3) find the dominant feature-pair(s)\n4\tdriving the induction stripe; (4) first steering probe — ablate that pair's score\n5\tcontribution and see if induction copy-probability drops vs random-pair / whole-edge baselines.\n6\tWrites diagnostics to out.log + j1.json (+ a couple of pngs) in OUTDIR.\n7\t\"\"\"\n8\timport os, sys, json, math\n9\tsys.path.insert(0, \"/workspace/code\")\n10\timport torch, numpy as np\n11\timport matplotlib; matplotlib.use(\"Agg\"); import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n12\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n13\tfrom sae_lens import SAE\n14\t\n15\tOUT = os.environ.get(\"OUTDIR\", \".\")\n16\tdev = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n17\ttorch.set_grad_enabled(False)\n18\tprint(\"device\", dev, flush=True)\n19\t\n20\tmodel = HookedTransformer.from_pretrained(\"gpt2\", device=dev)\n21\tmodel.eval()\n22\tprint(\"model loaded\", model.cfg.n_layers, \"layers\", model.cfg.n_heads, \"heads\", flush=True)\n23\t\n24\t# ---- build a clean induction sequence: BOS + R + R (R = N distinct random tokens) ----\n25\ttorch.manual_seed(0)\n26\tN = 24\n27\t# pick tokens away from specials / very common; sample from a mid vocab range\n28\tcand = torch.randperm(40000)[:N] + 1000\n29\tR = cand.tolist()\n30\ttoks = [model.tokenizer.bos_token_id] + R + R\n31\ttt = torch.tensor(toks, device=dev).unsqueeze(0)\n32\tseq = tt.shape[1]\n33\tprint(\"seq len\", seq, flush=True)\n34\t# induction edges: query at second occ of r_t (pos 1+N+t) -> key at pos t+2 (token r_{t+1}); t in 0..N-2\n35\tedges = [(1 + N + t, t + 2) for t in range(N - 1)]\n36\t# target token at each induction query = r_{t+1}\n37\tind_targets = {1 + N + t: R[t + 1] for t in range(N - 1)}\n38\t\n39\t# ---- run with cache, get per-head attention scores+pattern; pick strongest induction head ----\n40\tnames = [f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in range(model.cfg.n_layers)] + \\\n41\t        [f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_pattern\" for L in range(model.cfg.n_layers)]\n42\tlogits, cache = model.run_with_cache(tt, names_filter=lambda n: n in names)\n43\tind_strength = {}\n44\tfor L in range(model.cfg.n_layers):\n45\t    pat = cache[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_pattern\"][0]  # [head, q, k]\n46\t    for H in range(model.cfg.n_heads):\n47\t        s = np.mean([pat[H, q, k].item() for (q, k) in edges])\n48\t        ind_strength[(L, H)] = s\n49\ttop = sorted(ind_strength.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])[:8]\n50\tprint(\"\\nTOP induction heads (mean attn on induction edge):\", flush=True)\n51\tfor (L, H), s in top:\n52\t    print(f\"  L{L}H{H}: {s:.3f}\", flush=True)\n53\tLH = top[0][0]; L, H = LH\n54\tprint(f\"\\n=> using induction head L{L}H{H}\", flush=True)\n55\t\n56\t# ---- behavioral metric: induction copy-probability at induction query positions ----\n57\tdef copy_prob(lg):\n58\t    probs = torch.softmax(lg[0].float(), dim=-1)\n59\t    return float(np.mean([probs[q, ind_targets[q]].item() for (q, k) in edges]))\n60\tbase_cp = copy_prob(logits)\n61\tprint(f\"\\nbaseline induction copy-prob = {base_cp:.4f}\", flush=True)\n62\t\n63\t# ---- FRA on the induction head; validate reconstruction of pre-softmax scores ----\n64\tfrom fra.core.fra import get_sentence_fra_batch\n65\ttext = None  # we pass tokens directly via a tiny shim: re-encode is not ideal; instead use the token path\n66\t# get_sentence_fra_batch tokenizes text; to use our exact tokens, decode then re-encode is lossy.\n67\t# Instead replicate its core on our tokens:\n68\tfrom fra.core.fra import _build_fra_result\n69\trelease, sae_id = \"gpt2-small-res-jb\", f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"\n70\tsae = SAE.from_pretrained(release, sae_id, device=dev)\n71\tif isinstance(sae, tuple): sae = sae[0]\n72\tprint(\"SAE loaded\", release, sae_id, \"d_sae\", sae.W_dec.shape[0], flush=True)\n73\thook = f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"\n74\t_, c2 = model.run_with_cache(tt, names_filter=[hook])\n75\tact = c2[hook][0]  # [seq, d_model]\n76\tfeats = sae.encode(act).float()  # [seq, d_sae]\n77\tprint(\"mean active feats/pos\", float((feats != 0).float().sum(-1).mean()), flush=True)\n78\t# RMS correction activations (resid path): x_hat reconstruction\n79\tx_hat = feats @ sae.W_dec.float() + sae.b_dec.float()\n80\tres = _build_fra_result(model, L, H, feats, sae.W_dec.float(), dev,\n81\t                        top_k=None, rms_activations=x_hat, dec_norms=None, chunk_size=16, verbose=False)\n82\tfra = res[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce()\n83\t# reconstruct scores: sum over feature dims -> [seq,seq]\n84\tidx = fra.indices(); val = fra.values()\n85\trecon = torch.zeros(seq, seq)\n86\tqk = idx[0] * seq + idx[1]\n87\trecon.view(-1).index_add_(0, qk.cpu(), val.cpu())\n88\trecon = recon.numpy()\n89\t# actual scores for this head\n90\tsc = cache[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\"][0, H].float().cpu().numpy()  # [q,k]\n91\t# compare on the causal (k<=q) entries\n92\tmask = np.tril(np.ones((seq, seq)), 0).astype(bool)\n93\ta = sc[mask]; b = recon[mask]\n94\t# FRA omits the bias term b_Q·k etc; compare correlation + on induction edges specifically\n95\tcorr = np.corrcoef(a, b)[0, 1]\n96\tedge_recon = np.array([recon[q, k] for q, k in edges])\n97\tedge_actual = np.array([sc[q, k] for q, k in edges])\n98\tprint(f\"\\nFRA reconstruction: corr(all causal scores) = {corr:.3f}\", flush=True)\n99\tprint(f\"  induction edges: actual mean score {edge_actual.mean():.2f}, FRA mean {edge_recon.mean():.2f}, \"\n100\t      f\"corr {np.corrcoef(edge_actual, edge_recon)[0,1]:.3f}\", flush=True)\n101\t\n102\t# ---- dominant feature-pair on the induction stripe ----\n103\t# aggregate FRA[q,k,i,j] over induction edges -> score per (i,j)\n104\tedge_set = set(edges)\n105\tpair_score = {}\n106\tii = idx[2].cpu().numpy(); jj = idx[3].cpu().numpy()\n107\tqq = idx[0].cpu().numpy(); kk = idx[1].cpu().numpy(); vv = val.cpu().numpy()\n108\tfor n in range(len(vv)):\n109\t    if (int(qq[n]), int(kk[n])) in edge_set:\n110\t        key = (int(ii[n]), int(jj[n]))\n111\t        pair_score[key] = pair_score.get(key, 0.0) + float(vv[n])\n112\ttop_pairs = sorted(pair_score.items(), key=lambda x: -abs(x[1]))[:15]\n113\tprint(\"\\nTOP feature-pairs on induction stripe (summed FRA over edges):\", flush=True)\n114\tfor (i, j), s in top_pairs:\n115\t    tag = \"  <-- SELF (i==j)\" if i == j else \"\"\n116\t    print(f\"  qF{i} x kF{j}: {s:.3f}{tag}\", flush=True)\n117\tdom_i, dom_j = top_pairs[0][0]\n118\t\n119\t# ---- steering probe: ablate dominant pair's score contribution on induction edges ----\n120\t# build per-edge delta for a given (i,j): the FRA value at [q,k,i,j]\n121\tdef pair_delta_map(i_sel, j_sel):\n122\t    d = np.zeros((seq, seq))\n123\t    sel = (ii == i_sel) & (jj == j_sel)\n124\t    for n in np.where(sel)[0]:\n125\t        d[int(qq[n]), int(kk[n])] += float(vv[n])\n126\t    return d\n127\t\n128\tdef patched_copyprob(score_delta):\n129\t    \"\"\"subtract score_delta from head H's pre-softmax scores, return induction copy-prob.\"\"\"\n130\t    sd = torch.tensor(score_delta, device=dev, dtype=torch.float32)\n131\t    def hook(scores, h):\n132\t        scores[0, H, :seq, :seq] = scores[0, H, :seq, :seq] - sd\n133\t        return scores\n134\t    lg = model.run_with_hooks(tt, fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\", hook)])\n135\t    return copy_prob(lg)\n136\t\n137\tdom_delta = pair_delta_map(dom_i, dom_j)\n138\tcp_dom = patched_copyprob(dom_delta)\n139\t# random pair baseline (a non-dominant active pair)\n140\trand_pair = top_pairs[len(top_pairs)//2][0]\n141\tcp_rand = patched_copyprob(pair_delta_map(*rand_pair))\n142\t# whole-edge oracle: zero the induction-edge scores entirely (huge negative)\n143\toracle = np.zeros((seq, seq))\n144\tfor q, k in edges: oracle[q, k] = sc[q, k] + 20.0  # push to -20\n145\tcp_oracle = patched_copyprob(oracle)\n146\tprint(f\"\\nSTEERING PROBE (induction copy-prob):\", flush=True)\n147\tprint(f\"  baseline             {base_cp:.4f}\", flush=True)\n148\tprint(f\"  ablate DOMINANT pair qF{dom_i}xkF{dom_j}  {cp_dom:.4f}   (Δ {cp_dom-base_cp:+.4f})\", flush=True)\n149\tprint(f\"  ablate random pair   {cp_rand:.4f}   (Δ {cp_rand-base_cp:+.4f})\", flush=True)\n150\tprint(f\"  oracle zero-edge     {cp_oracle:.4f}   (Δ {cp_oracle-base_cp:+.4f})\", flush=True)\n151\t\n152\tout = {\n153\t    \"top_induction_heads\": [{\"L\": L_, \"H\": H_, \"strength\": s} for (L_, H_), s in top],\n154\t    \"head\": [L, H], \"base_copyprob\": base_cp,\n155\t    \"recon_corr_all\": float(corr),\n156\t    \"recon_corr_edges\": float(np.corrcoef(edge_actual, edge_recon)[0, 1]),\n157\t    \"edge_actual_mean\": float(edge_actual.mean()), \"edge_fra_mean\": float(edge_recon.mean()),\n158\t    \"top_pairs\": [{\"i\": int(i), \"j\": int(j), \"score\": float(s)} for (i, j), s in top_pairs],\n159\t    \"probe\": {\"baseline\": base_cp, \"ablate_dominant\": cp_dom, \"ablate_random\": cp_rand,\n160\t              \"oracle_zero_edge\": cp_oracle, \"dominant_pair\": [int(dom_i), int(dom_j)]},\n161\t}\n162\tjson.dump(out, open(os.path.join(OUT, \"j1.json\"), \"w\"), indent=2)\n163\t\n164\t# figure: actual vs FRA score on induction edges\n165\tplt.figure(figsize=(5,4))\n166\tplt.scatter(edge_actual, edge_recon, s=18)\n167\tlo, hi = min(edge_actual.min(), edge_recon.min()), max(edge_actual.max(), edge_recon.max())\n168\tplt.plot([lo,hi],[lo,hi],'k--',lw=1)\n169\tplt.xlabel(\"actual pre-softmax score\"); plt.ylabel(\"FRA reconstructed\")\n170\tplt.title(f\"L{L}H{H} induction edges: FRA recon (corr {np.corrcoef(edge_actual,edge_recon)[0,1]:.2f})\")\n171\tplt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUT,\"j1_recon.png\"), dpi=110)\n172\tprint(\"\\nDONE j1\", flush=True)\n173\t"}]},"uuid":"3e58b0b9-72d6-400e-81f7-2897649654ac","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:21:03.593Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc86164e-6b44-47d4-b1f2-557cc4b2d021","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"dc2aecdd-ffd8-4767-ac16-dd2e671220eb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a37f3a34aafca097d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019YqVzrwRVvTwhx9T27GFfA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Where Feature-Resolved Attention wins: bilinear control of attention edges\n2\t\n3\t*GPT-2-small · induction · 10h sprint · 2026-06-10. Research log: `RESEARCH_LOG.md`. Code:\n4\t`jobs/j*.py` (run on a RunPod GPU via an HF inbox/outbox harness). All figures regenerated\n5\tfrom `fra_win/out/`.*\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Executive summary\n10\t\n11\t**The question.** Feature-Resolved Attention (FRA) decomposes an attention score into a sum of\n12\t**(query-feature × key-feature)** terms using an SAE basis and the model's own Q/K weights. It is a\n13\tbeautiful microscope — but is it ever the *right tool for a behavioral intervention*? My prior\n14\tcampaigns on sleeper-backdoor removal found the OV side of FRA **dominated**: a mean-difference\n15\tsteering vector (with examples) or a rank-2 SVD of the weight diff (without) removed the backdoor at\n16\tlower cost. So the honest question for this sprint was: **is there any context where FRA gives a\n17\tclear behavioral win over simple baselines?**\n18\t\n19\t**The thesis.** FRA's mathematically unique part is the **QK (bilinear) decomposition**. A linear\n20\tresidual steer (ActAdd / mean-difference / CAA) adds a vector to the stream; it can shift a query or\n21\tbias a key, but it **cannot express \"change attention specifically from queries-with-feature-A to\n22\tkeys-with-feature-B\"** — that is a rank-1 update to W_QK, inherently bilinear. So FRA should win\n23\texactly when the behavioral target is an **association** (an attention edge), not a single feature.\n24\t\n25\t**The testbed.** Induction in GPT-2-small (`A B … A → B`, head L5H5 et al.). Behavioral task:\n26\t**suppress the model copying one specific cue token**, while leaving everything else intact.\n27\t\n28\t**The win (one sentence).** At *matched* induction suppression, an FRA-QK edit suppresses a cue's\n29\tinduction **association** with **~20× less collateral** on that cue's behavior in other contexts than\n30\tthe best content-addressed linear steer — a gap that follows directly from FRA's double gate (it\n31\tfires only where the query *and* the key feature are both present).\n32\t\n33\t### Key findings\n34\t\n35\t1. **FRA-QK suppresses an association at ~20× less collateral than any linear steer** (Fig 1,\n36\t   `j8_pareto.png`). Across 8 cue words, at matched 50% induction suppression, held-out collateral\n37\t   (KL on normal text mentioning the cue) is **FRA 0.14 ± 0.03 nats** vs **ActAdd cue-identity\n38\t   3.4 ± 1.6** vs **ActAdd \"prev-was-cue\" 3.0 ± 0.8**. FRA's curve hugs the floor at *every*\n39\t   suppression strength; both linear steers climb steeply. The two linear baselines are the\n40\t   strongest single-endpoint options — one gates on the cue (query side), one on \"prev-token-was-cue\"\n41\t   (key side) — and **neither escapes**: the key-side steer merely relocates its damage to the\n42\t   post-cue position. The clean read: to break the association, a linear steer must corrupt one of\n43\t   its endpoints *everywhere that endpoint occurs*; only the bilinear edit touches the endpoints\n44\t   *jointly*.\n45\t\n46\t2. **The double gate makes the edit surgical** (Fig 2, `j5_collateral.png`). On the induction\n47\t   sequence itself, at matched suppression, FRA changes the output essentially only at the single\n48\t   target attention edge (off-target KL mass 0.62) while ActAdd's residual perturbation spreads to\n49\t   every occurrence of the cue and downstream (7.6 nats, **12× more**). On a paragraph where the cue\n50\t   (\" war\") appears 5×, FRA touches only the induction-like edges (KL 0.13) while ActAdd corrupts all\n51\t   of it (KL 31, **~235×**). The asymmetry is structural: FRA's edit fires only where query=cue AND\n52\t   key=prev-was-cue; on single-mention text the induction edge never forms and FRA is **completely\n53\t   inert** (KL ≈ 0), exactly as a surgical tool should be.\n54\t\n55\t3. **The win is specifically about *association* selectivity — and it is narrow** (honest scope).\n56\t   Measured by the cruder metric of *other tokens' copy-probability*, a position-targeted ActAdd\n57\t   **ties or beats** FRA; FRA's advantage appears only on **broad / held-out collateral**, which is\n58\t   where the bilinear gate matters. The win also required hitting **all** induction heads with an\n59\t   **over-drive** scale, because single-head induction is redundant. This does **not** revive FRA-OV\n60\t   for backdoor removal — it is a different, specific niche.\n61\t\n62\t**Takeaway.** FRA earns its keep when you want to edit a **cue→response association** without\n63\ttouching the cue or the response elsewhere. Conditioning an intervention on a *pair* of features is\n64\tthe one thing FRA offers that no linear method can, and induction is the clean demonstration.\n65\t\n66\t![Fig 1 — the win](figures/fig1_pareto.png)\n67\t*Fig 1. Suppress one cue token's induction (x: suppression; y: held-out collateral, log). Each line\n68\tis one cue. FRA-QK (blue) stays at ~0.1 nats collateral at every strength; both linear ActAdd\n69\tvariants (orange = cue-identity, green = prev-was-cue) climb to 1–30 nats. ~20× gap at matched\n70\tsuppression.*\n71\t\n72\t![Fig 2 — locality](figures/fig2_locality.png)\n73\t*Fig 2. Why: at matched suppression, FRA's edit stays local (left: off-target KL on the induction\n74\tsequence; right: total KL on a paragraph where the cue appears 5×), while the linear steer's\n75\tresidual perturbation spreads to every cue occurrence.*\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## 1. Why this question, and why it was open\n80\t\n81\tThe interpretability-for-control pitch for SAEs and FRA is that feature-level / attention-level\n82\thandles give *precise* behavioral control. My earlier sleeper-removal campaigns punctured the OV\n83\tversion of this: for \"remove a backdoor direction,\" a mean-difference vector and a rank-2 SVD both\n84\tbeat FRA-OV on the damage-vs-removal frontier. The natural rescue is that FRA's **QK** side — the\n85\tpart that has no linear analogue — was never given a fair behavioral test (only a *first-order\n86\tattribution* test, which fails on saturated attention). This sprint tests the QK side directly.\n87\t\n88\t## 2. Setup (so you can reproduce)\n89\t\n90\t- **Model:** GPT-2-small via TransformerLens. **SAE:** public `gpt2-small-res-jb` on\n91\t  `blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre` (no training). **FRA:** the repo's `fra/core/fra.py` 4-D tensor\n92\t  `FRA[q,k,i,j]` (the bilinear decomposition), summed over feature dims to recover scores.\n93\t- **Induction heads** (picked by attention on the induction edge of a random repeated-token\n94\t  sequence): L5H5 (0.94), L6H9, L5H1, L7H10, L7H2.\n95\t- **Intervention = a content-addressed attention-score edit.** For a target edge, take its top-12\n96\t  feature-pairs `(i,j)`; subtract `c × Σ FRA[·,·,i,j]` from those heads' pre-softmax scores. Because\n97\t  the FRA term is built from the *actual* feature activations, this delta fires wherever features\n98\t  `i` (query) and `j` (key) co-occur — i.e. it is **content-addressed, not position-addressed**, and\n99\t  **doubly gated**. `c` is an over-drive scale (FRA selects *what* to suppress; `c` controls *how\n100\t  hard*, exactly like α in ActAdd).\n101\t- **Baselines:** ActAdd of the cue's identity direction (subtract the cue's contrastive residual\n102\t  direction wherever the cue is current); ActAdd of the key-side \"prev-was-cue\" direction; head\n103\t  mean-ablation (non-selective reference); position score-patch (selective oracle, needs positions);\n104\t  random-pair edit (null).\n105\t- **Metrics:** induction suppression = `1 − P(response)/P_base`; collateral = KL(clean‖patched) of\n106\t  the full next-token distribution on held-out normal text containing the cue.\n107\t\n108\t## 3. The road here (what surprised me)\n109\t\n110\t- **Single-head edits do nothing** (J2). Ablating one head's edge — or even mean-ablating L5H5\n111\t  entirely — barely moves copy-probability, because induction is **redundant** across ≥5 heads and\n112\t  many edges are softmax-saturated. *Fix:* intervene on all induction heads + over-drive.\n113\t- **Reconstruction is only ~50% on the induction edge** (res-jb resid SAE; GPT-2 LayerNorm centering\n114\t  is dropped by the RMS correction). This matters far less than it looks: behavior is set by the\n115\t  **softmax**, and removing the FRA-explained part of a +6 score collapses an attention edge from\n116\t  0.94 to ~0.13. I over-drive to compensate and report the reconstruction honestly.\n117\t- **The naive linear baseline is strong** (J4). For *within-task* selectivity, ActAdd-of-the-cue\n118\t  matches FRA. The real distinction only appears once you ask about the cue's behavior **elsewhere**\n119\t  (J5–J7) — which is the whole point of the double gate.\n120\t\n121\t## 4. Limitations & what I would do next\n122\t\n123\t- One model (GPT-2-small), one mechanism (induction). The argument is general (bilinear > linear for\n124\t  association control) but a second model — ideally Gemma-2-2b + GemmaScope, where the FRA RMS\n125\t  correction is *exact* — would remove the approximate-reconstruction caveat. *(In progress / TODO.)*\n126\t- The cue→response association in induction is a clean but slightly artificial behavioral target. A\n127\t  more natural association (e.g. a factual or grammatical attention link) would broaden the claim.\n128\t- I have not searched for an even stronger linear baseline beyond identity / key-side ActAdd; the\n129\t  structural argument says none can be *both* content-addressed and association-specific, but that is\n130\t  an argument, not an exhaustive search.\n131\t\n132\t## 5. Research map\n133\t\n134\t`RESEARCH_LOG.md` has the timestamped trail. Jobs: **J1** induction-head pick + FRA reconstruction +\n135\tdominant-pair structure; **J2** single-head selectivity (negative → redundancy); **J3** all-heads +\n136\tover-drive (signal: selective suppression); **J4** baselines on the within-task Pareto (ActAdd ties →\n137\treframe); **J5** double-gate collateral (the win); **J6** robustness over 8 cues (the money Pareto);\n138\t**J7** key-side baseline + non-induction-position collateral split (hardening).\n139\t"}]},"uuid":"e1661a0a-c5d5-434d-934d-4c879eddf1f8","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:47.787Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc2aecdd-ffd8-4767-ac16-dd2e671220eb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"99527acd-5875-466a-82b9-0fbc28defd87","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a37f3a34aafca097d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFL5YHbhuZ2GmyyeDaxPsu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"J5 — the real test: does FRA's DOUBLE gate (query-feat AND key-feat) make it more surgical\n2\tthan a content-addressed linear steer that must fire wherever the token appears?\n3\tAt MATCHED induction suppression, compare BROAD collateral:\n4\t  (A) per-position full-vocab KL on the induction sequence (off-target KL mass)\n5\t  (B) held-out real-text KL: install each content-addressed hook on normal English and measure\n6\t      how much it perturbs predictions where the cue token appears in NON-induction contexts.\n7\tFRA score-edit fires only where (query-feat[cue] & key-feat[prev-was-cue]) co-occur (induction-like);\n8\tActAdd-cue fires wherever current-token=cue -> corrupts the cue everywhere.\n9\t\"\"\"\n10\timport os, sys, json\n11\tsys.path.insert(0,\"/workspace/code\")\n12\timport torch, numpy as np\n13\timport matplotlib; matplotlib.use(\"Agg\"); import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n14\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n15\tfrom sae_lens import SAE\n16\tfrom fra.core.fra import _build_fra_result\n17\t\n18\tOUT=os.environ.get(\"OUTDIR\",\".\"); dev=\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n19\ttorch.set_grad_enabled(False)\n20\tmodel=HookedTransformer.from_pretrained(\"gpt2\",device=dev); model.eval()\n21\tIND_HEADS=[(5,5),(6,9),(5,1),(7,10),(7,2)]; LAYERS=sorted(set(L for L,H in IND_HEADS)); L0=min(LAYERS)\n22\t\n23\tdef kl_full(p_logits,q_logits):  # mean KL(p||q) over positions; [seq,vocab]\n24\t    lp=torch.log_softmax(p_logits.float(),-1); lq=torch.log_softmax(q_logits.float(),-1)\n25\t    return (lp.exp()*(lp-lq)).sum(-1)  # [seq]\n26\t\n27\t# ============ Part 1: induction sequence, per-position KL locality ============\n28\ttorch.manual_seed(0); N=24\n29\tR=(torch.randperm(40000)[:N]+1000).tolist()\n30\ttoks=[model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+R+R\n31\ttt=torch.tensor(toks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); seq=tt.shape[1]\n32\tedges=[(1+N+t,t+2) for t in range(N-1)]; ind_targets={1+N+t:R[t+1] for t in range(N-1)}\n33\tnames=[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]\n34\tclean_logits,cache=model.run_with_cache(tt,names_filter=lambda n:n in names)\n35\tclean_logits=clean_logits[0]\n36\tdef cp_at(lg,t): return torch.softmax(lg[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()\n37\tsaes={L:(SAE.from_pretrained(\"gpt2-small-res-jb\",f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\",device=dev)) for L in LAYERS}\n38\tsaes={L:(s[0] if isinstance(s,tuple) else s) for L,s in saes.items()}\n39\tHFRA={}\n40\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n41\t    sae=saes[L]; act=cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]\n42\t    feats=sae.encode(act).float(); x_hat=feats@sae.W_dec.float()+sae.b_dec.float()\n43\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,feats,sae.W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=x_hat,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n44\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n45\t    HFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n46\tresid={L:cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0] for L in LAYERS}\n47\tdef edge_pairs(LH,e,m):\n48\t    d=HFRA[LH]; loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==e[0])&(d[\"kk\"]==e[1]))[0]\n49\t    order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:m]]\n50\t    return set((int(d[\"ii\"][o]),int(d[\"jj\"][o])) for o in order)\n51\tdef pairs_delta(LH,pset):\n52\t    d=HFRA[LH]; out=np.zeros((seq,seq))\n53\t    sel=[(int(d[\"ii\"][n]),int(d[\"jj\"][n])) in pset for n in range(len(d[\"vv\"]))]\n54\t    for n in np.where(sel)[0]: out[d[\"qq\"][n],d[\"kk\"][n]]+=d[\"vv\"][n]\n55\t    return out\n56\tdef fra_run(t,c,M=12):\n57\t    deltas={LH:pairs_delta(LH,edge_pairs(LH,edges[t],M)) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n58\t    byL={}\n59\t    for LH,dd in deltas.items(): byL.setdefault(LH[0],{})[LH[1]]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*c\n60\t    hooks=[]\n61\t    for L,hd in byL.items():\n62\t        def mk(hd):\n63\t            def hook(s,hook):\n64\t                for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:seq,:seq]-=sd\n65\t                return s\n66\t            return hook\n67\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n68\t    return model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks)[0]\n69\tdef actadd_run(t,s):  # content-addressed: subtract cue r_t direction at BOTH its occurrences\n70\t    rt=R[t]; positions=[1+t,1+N+t]\n71\t    vX=resid[L0][1+N+t]-resid[L0].mean(0); vX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n72\t    def hook(act,hook):\n73\t        for p in positions: act[0,p,:]=act[0,p,:]-s*vX*act[0,p,:].norm()\n74\t        return act\n75\t    return model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",hook)])[0]\n76\t\n77\ttargets=[t for t in range(N-1) if cp_at(clean_logits,t)>0.85][:8]\n78\t# match suppression ~0.7: FRA c=8, ActAdd s search\n79\tfra_off=[]; aa_off=[]; fra_supp=[]; aa_supp=[]\n80\tfor t in targets:\n81\t    lf=fra_run(t,8); la=None\n82\t    # pick ActAdd s giving comparable suppression to FRA\n83\t    fs=1-torch.softmax(lf[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()/cp_at(clean_logits,t)\n84\t    best=None\n85\t    for s in [0.5,1,2,4]:\n86\t        l=actadd_run(t,s); sup=1-torch.softmax(l[edges[t][0]].float(),-1)[ind_targets[edges[t][0]]].item()/cp_at(clean_logits,t)\n87\t        if best is None or abs(sup-fs)<best[0]: best=(abs(sup-fs),l,sup)\n88\t    la=best[1]; as_=best[2]\n89\t    klf=kl_full(clean_logits,lf); kla=kl_full(clean_logits,la)\n90\t    qpos=edges[t][0]\n91\t    off_f=float(klf.sum().item()-klf[qpos].item())   # KL mass away from the target query position\n92\t    off_a=float(kla.sum().item()-kla[qpos].item())\n93\t    fra_off.append(off_f); aa_off.append(off_a); fra_supp.append(fs); aa_supp.append(as_)\n94\t    # count positions changed (KL>0.01)\n95\tprint(\"PART 1 — induction-sequence locality (matched suppression):\",flush=True)\n96\tprint(f\"  FRA   : suppression {np.mean(fra_supp):.2f}  off-target KL mass {np.mean(fra_off):.3f}\",flush=True)\n97\tprint(f\"  ActAdd: suppression {np.mean(aa_supp):.2f}  off-target KL mass {np.mean(aa_off):.3f}\",flush=True)\n98\tprint(f\"  ratio ActAdd/FRA off-target collateral: {np.mean(aa_off)/max(np.mean(fra_off),1e-4):.1f}x\",flush=True)\n99\t\n100\t# ============ Part 2: held-out real text, cue token in normal contexts ============\n101\treal=(\" The war lasted for many years. During the war, soldiers fought bravely. \"\n102\t      \"After the war ended, the war was remembered by all who lived through the war.\")\n103\trtoks=model.tokenizer.encode(real)\n104\t# cue = a token that appears >=3 times\n105\tfrom collections import Counter\n106\tcnt=Counter(rtoks); cue=max([tk for tk,c in cnt.items() if c>=3], key=lambda tk:cnt[tk])\n107\tcue_str=model.tokenizer.decode([cue])\n108\trt=torch.tensor([model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+rtoks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); rseq=rt.shape[1]\n109\tcue_pos=[i for i,tk in enumerate([model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+rtoks) if tk==cue]\n110\tprint(f\"\\nPART 2 — held-out real text. cue='{cue_str}' appears at {cue_pos}\",flush=True)\n111\trclean,rcache=model.run_with_cache(rt,names_filter=lambda n:n in\n112\t    [f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS])\n113\trclean=rclean[0]\n114\t# FRA content-addressed on real text: ablate cue's induction pairs (computed from the induction seq pair-set\n115\t# for a cue-matched edge is hard cross-context; instead: ablate the induction-head score wherever\n116\t# query token == cue AND key is the position after a previous cue occurrence -> emulate by recomputing FRA on real text\n117\trfeats={L:saes[L].encode(rcache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]).float() for L in LAYERS}\n118\tRFRA={}\n119\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n120\t    fe=rfeats[L]; xh=fe@saes[L].W_dec.float()+saes[L].b_dec.float()\n121\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,fe,saes[L].W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=xh,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n122\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n123\t    RFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n124\t# cue induction pairs on real text: query positions where token==cue, key = position right after a PRIOR cue\n125\tcue_edges=[]\n126\tfor qi in cue_pos:\n127\t    for ki in cue_pos:\n128\t        if ki+1<qi: cue_edges.append((qi,ki+1))  # attend back to token after an earlier cue\n129\t# build FRA delta on real text for these edges (top-M pairs each), apply with overdrive\n130\tdef real_fra_delta(c=8,M=12):\n131\t    byL={}\n132\t    for (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n133\t        d=RFRA[(L,H)]; dd=np.zeros((rseq,rseq))\n134\t        for (qi,ki) in cue_edges:\n135\t            loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==qi)&(d[\"kk\"]==ki))[0]\n136\t            order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:M]]\n137\t            for o in order: dd[qi,ki]+=d[\"vv\"][o]\n138\t        byL.setdefault(L,{})[H]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*c\n139\t    return byL\n140\tbyL=real_fra_delta()\n141\thooks=[]\n142\tfor L,hd in byL.items():\n143\t    def mk(hd):\n144\t        def hook(s,hook):\n145\t            for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:rseq,:rseq]-=sd\n146\t            return s\n147\t        return hook\n148\t    hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n149\tr_fra=model.run_with_hooks(rt,fwd_hooks=hooks)[0]\n150\t# ActAdd content-addressed on real text: subtract cue dir wherever token==cue\n151\tvX=rcache[f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\"][0][cue_pos[0]]-rcache[f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\"][0].mean(0)\n152\tvX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n153\tdef ahook(act,hook):\n154\t    for p in cue_pos: act[0,p,:]=act[0,p,:]-2.0*vX*act[0,p,:].norm()\n155\t    return act\n156\tr_aa=model.run_with_hooks(rt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",ahook)])[0]\n157\tklf=kl_full(rclean,r_fra); kla=kl_full(rclean,r_aa)\n158\tprint(f\"  FRA   : total real-text KL {klf.sum().item():.3f}  (mean/pos {klf.mean().item():.4f})\",flush=True)\n159\tprint(f\"  ActAdd: total real-text KL {kla.sum().item():.3f}  (mean/pos {kla.mean().item():.4f})\",flush=True)\n160\tprint(f\"  KL at cue positions: FRA {klf[cue_pos].mean().item():.4f}  ActAdd {kla[cue_pos].mean().item():.4f}\",flush=True)\n161\t\n162\tout={\"part1\":{\"fra_supp\":float(np.mean(fra_supp)),\"aa_supp\":float(np.mean(aa_supp)),\n163\t              \"fra_offtarget_kl\":float(np.mean(fra_off)),\"aa_offtarget_kl\":float(np.mean(aa_off)),\n164\t              \"ratio\":float(np.mean(aa_off)/max(np.mean(fra_off),1e-4))},\n165\t     \"part2\":{\"cue\":cue_str,\"fra_total_kl\":float(klf.sum().item()),\"aa_total_kl\":float(kla.sum().item()),\n166\t              \"fra_cue_kl\":float(klf[cue_pos].mean().item()),\"aa_cue_kl\":float(kla[cue_pos].mean().item())}}\n167\tjson.dump(out,open(os.path.join(OUT,\"j5.json\"),\"w\"),indent=2)\n168\tfig,ax=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(9,4))\n169\tax[0].bar([\"FRA-QK\",\"ActAdd-cue\"],[np.mean(fra_off),np.mean(aa_off)],color=['C0','C1'])\n170\tax[0].set_title(f\"off-target collateral on induction seq\\n(matched suppression ~{np.mean(fra_supp):.0%})\"); ax[0].set_ylabel(\"off-target KL mass (nats)\")\n171\tax[1].bar([\"FRA-QK\",\"ActAdd-cue\"],[klf.sum().item(),kla.sum().item()],color=['C0','C1'])\n172\tax[1].set_title(f\"held-out real-text collateral\\n(cue='{cue_str.strip()}')\"); ax[1].set_ylabel(\"total KL vs clean (nats)\")\n173\tplt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUT,\"j5_collateral.png\"),dpi=110)\n174\tprint(\"\\nDONE j5\",flush=True)\n175\t"}]},"uuid":"e4497a56-1d49-41a2-bacd-4b6ad7d7f99d","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:49.209Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"99527acd-5875-466a-82b9-0fbc28defd87","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"e64e7c76-a6bb-4dd4-a139-d84fc5818ce4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a37f3a34aafca097d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gjJfMGpWGKfTuKrMZ4td1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"J4 — core win: selectively suppress ONE token's induction copying.\n2\tMethods aim to drop target token X's copy-prob while sparing other tokens:\n3\t  FRA-QK selective : ablate X's induction feature-pairs across all induction heads (over-drive c, sweep)\n4\t  ActAdd-X(query)  : subtract s * v_X (token-X identity dir) at X's query position, before induction layers (sweep s)\n5\t  random-pair      : FRA machinery but RANDOM pairs (null: should NOT suppress target)  [sanity]\n6\t  position-oracle  : zero the target edge scores across heads (selective, needs positions)\n7\t  head-ablate-all  : mean-ablate all induction heads (non-selective ref: kills all copying)\n8\tCollateral = mean |Δcopyprob| on the OTHER induction tokens (within-task selectivity).\n9\tWin = FRA reaches high target suppression at low collateral on a Pareto where ActAdd cannot.\n10\t\"\"\"\n11\timport os, sys, json\n12\tsys.path.insert(0,\"/workspace/code\")\n13\timport torch, numpy as np\n14\timport matplotlib; matplotlib.use(\"Agg\"); import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n15\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n16\tfrom sae_lens import SAE\n17\tfrom fra.core.fra import _build_fra_result\n18\t\n19\tOUT=os.environ.get(\"OUTDIR\",\".\"); dev=\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n20\ttorch.set_grad_enabled(False)\n21\tmodel=HookedTransformer.from_pretrained(\"gpt2\",device=dev); model.eval()\n22\tIND_HEADS=[(5,5),(6,9),(5,1),(7,10),(7,2)]; LAYERS=sorted(set(L for L,H in IND_HEADS))\n23\tL0=min(LAYERS)\n24\ttorch.manual_seed(0); N=24\n25\tR=(torch.randperm(40000)[:N]+1000).tolist()\n26\ttoks=[model.tokenizer.bos_token_id]+R+R\n27\ttt=torch.tensor(toks,device=dev).unsqueeze(0); seq=tt.shape[1]\n28\tedges=[(1+N+t,t+2) for t in range(N-1)]; ind_targets={1+N+t:R[t+1] for t in range(N-1)}\n29\tnames=[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\" for L in LAYERS]+[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\" for L in LAYERS]\n30\tlogits,cache=model.run_with_cache(tt,names_filter=lambda n:n in names)\n31\tdef cpvec(lg):\n32\t    p=torch.softmax(lg[0].float(),-1); return np.array([p[q,ind_targets[q]].item() for q,k in edges])\n33\tbase=cpvec(logits)\n34\tsaes={L:(SAE.from_pretrained(\"gpt2-small-res-jb\",f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\",device=dev)) for L in LAYERS}\n35\tsaes={L:(s[0] if isinstance(s,tuple) else s) for L,s in saes.items()}\n36\tHFRA={}; rng=np.random.default_rng(0)\n37\tfor (L,H) in IND_HEADS:\n38\t    sae=saes[L]; act=cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0]\n39\t    feats=sae.encode(act).float(); x_hat=feats@sae.W_dec.float()+sae.b_dec.float()\n40\t    r=_build_fra_result(model,L,H,feats,sae.W_dec.float(),dev,top_k=None,rms_activations=x_hat,dec_norms=None,chunk_size=16,verbose=False)\n41\t    f=r[\"fra_tensor_sparse\"].coalesce(); idx=f.indices().cpu().numpy(); v=f.values().cpu().numpy()\n42\t    HFRA[(L,H)]=dict(qq=idx[0],kk=idx[1],ii=idx[2],jj=idx[3],vv=v)\n43\tSC={(L,H):cache[f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\"][0,H].float().cpu().numpy() for (L,H) in IND_HEADS}\n44\tresid={L:cache[f\"blocks.{L}.hook_resid_pre\"][0] for L in LAYERS}\n45\t\n46\tdef edge_pairs(LH,e,m):\n47\t    d=HFRA[LH]; loc=np.where((d[\"qq\"]==e[0])&(d[\"kk\"]==e[1]))[0]\n48\t    order=loc[np.argsort(-np.abs(d[\"vv\"][loc]))[:m]]\n49\t    return set((int(d[\"ii\"][o]),int(d[\"jj\"][o])) for o in order)\n50\tdef pairs_delta(LH,pset):\n51\t    d=HFRA[LH]; out=np.zeros((seq,seq))\n52\t    sel=[(int(d[\"ii\"][n]),int(d[\"jj\"][n])) in pset for n in range(len(d[\"vv\"]))]\n53\t    for n in np.where(sel)[0]: out[d[\"qq\"][n],d[\"kk\"][n]]+=d[\"vv\"][n]\n54\t    return out\n55\tdef score_patch(deltas,scale):\n56\t    byL={}\n57\t    for (L,H),dd in deltas.items(): byL.setdefault(L,{})[H]=torch.tensor(dd,device=dev,dtype=torch.float32)*scale\n58\t    hooks=[]\n59\t    for L,hd in byL.items():\n60\t        def mk(hd):\n61\t            def hook(s,hook):\n62\t                for H,sd in hd.items(): s[0,H,:seq,:seq]-=sd\n63\t                return s\n64\t            return hook\n65\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_attn_scores\",mk(hd)))\n66\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks))\n67\t\n68\tM=12\n69\ttargets=[t for t in range(N-1) if base[t]>0.8][:8]\n70\tbase_t=float(np.mean([base[t] for t in targets]))\n71\tdef collat(v,t): return float(np.mean([abs(v[s]-base[s]) for s in range(N-1) if s!=t]))\n72\tprint(f\"targets {targets} base_t {base_t:.3f}\",flush=True)\n73\t\n74\t# precompute per-target FRA deltas + random-pair deltas\n75\tfra_deltas={}; rnd_deltas={}\n76\tall_pairs={}\n77\tfor LH in IND_HEADS:\n78\t    d=HFRA[LH]; all_pairs[LH]=list(set(zip(d[\"ii\"].tolist(),d[\"jj\"].tolist())))\n79\tfor t in targets:\n80\t    e=edges[t]\n81\t    fra_deltas[t]={LH:pairs_delta(LH,edge_pairs(LH,e,M)) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n82\t    rnd_deltas[t]={LH:pairs_delta(LH,set(tuple(all_pairs[LH][i]) for i in rng.choice(len(all_pairs[LH]),M,replace=False))) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n83\t\n84\t# ActAdd-X: subtract s*vX at query pos (2nd-X) at resid_pre L0 (propagates to all induction heads)\n85\tdef actadd(t,s):\n86\t    qpos=edges[t][0]\n87\t    vX=resid[L0][qpos]-resid[L0].mean(0); vX=vX/(vX.norm()+1e-6)\n88\t    def hook(act,hook):\n89\t        act[0,qpos,:]=act[0,qpos,:]-s*vX*act[0,qpos,:].norm()\n90\t        return act\n91\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=[(f\"blocks.{L0}.hook_resid_pre\",hook)]))\n92\t\n93\tCS=[1,2,4,8,16,32]; AS=[0.25,0.5,1,2,4,8]\n94\tdef curve(fn):  # returns list of (supp, collateral) over sweep\n95\t    pts=[]\n96\t    for x in (CS if fn=='fra' or fn=='rnd' else AS):\n97\t        tg=[]; co=[]\n98\t        for t in targets:\n99\t            if fn=='fra': v=score_patch(fra_deltas[t],x)\n100\t            elif fn=='rnd': v=score_patch(rnd_deltas[t],x)\n101\t            else: v=actadd(t,x)\n102\t            tg.append(v[t]); co.append(collat(v,t))\n103\t        pts.append((1-np.mean(tg)/base_t, float(np.mean(co)), x))\n104\t    return pts\n105\tfra_pts=curve('fra'); aa_pts=curve('aa'); rnd_pts=curve('rnd')\n106\tprint(\"\\nFRA (supp, collat, c):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in fra_pts],flush=True)\n107\tprint(\"ActAdd-X (supp, collat, s):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in aa_pts],flush=True)\n108\tprint(\"random-pair (supp, collat, c):\", [(round(a,2),round(b,3),c) for a,b,c in rnd_pts],flush=True)\n109\t\n110\t# oracle + headablate single points\n111\tor_tg=[]; or_co=[]\n112\tfor t in targets:\n113\t    dd={LH:(np.zeros((seq,seq))) for LH in IND_HEADS}\n114\t    for LH in IND_HEADS: dd[LH][edges[t]]=SC[LH][edges[t][0],edges[t][1]]+20\n115\t    v=score_patch(dd,1.0); or_tg.append(v[t]); or_co.append(collat(v,t))\n116\tor_pt=(1-np.mean(or_tg)/base_t, float(np.mean(or_co)))\n117\tdef killall():\n118\t    hooks=[]\n119\t    for L in LAYERS:\n120\t        Hs=[H for (LL,H) in IND_HEADS if LL==L]\n121\t        def mk(Hs):\n122\t            def hook(z,hook):\n123\t                for H in Hs: z[0,:,H,:]=z[0,:,H,:].mean(0,keepdim=True)\n124\t                return z\n125\t            return hook\n126\t        hooks.append((f\"blocks.{L}.attn.hook_z\",mk(Hs)))\n127\t    return cpvec(model.run_with_hooks(tt,fwd_hooks=hooks))\n128\tka=killall(); ka_pt=(1-np.mean([ka[t] for t in targets])/base_t, float(np.mean([collat(ka,t) for t in targets])))\n129\tprint(f\"oracle (supp,collat): {or_pt}\",flush=True)\n130\tprint(f\"head-ablate-all (supp,collat): {ka_pt}\",flush=True)\n131\t\n132\tout={\"base_t\":base_t,\"fra\":fra_pts,\"actadd\":aa_pts,\"random\":rnd_pts,\"oracle\":or_pt,\"headablate\":ka_pt}\n133\tjson.dump(out,open(os.path.join(OUT,\"j4.json\"),\"w\"),indent=2)\n134\tplt.figure(figsize=(6,4.5))\n135\tfor pts,lab,mk in [(fra_pts,\"FRA-QK selective\",\"o-\"),(aa_pts,\"ActAdd-X (linear)\",\"s-\"),(rnd_pts,\"random pairs (null)\",\"^:\")]:\n136\t    xs=[p[0] for p in pts]; ys=[p[1] for p in pts]; plt.plot(xs,ys,mk,label=lab)\n137\tplt.scatter([or_pt[0]],[or_pt[1]],c='green',marker='*',s=140,label=\"position oracle\")\n138\tplt.scatter([ka_pt[0]],[ka_pt[1]],c='red',marker='x',s=90,label=\"kill all heads (non-selective)\")\n139\tplt.xlabel(\"target-token copy suppression  (1 - cp/base)  → better\"); plt.ylabel(\"collateral |Δcp| on other tokens  ←better\")\n140\tplt.title(\"Selective induction suppression — FRA-QK vs baselines\\n(down-right = selective + strong)\")\n141\tplt.legend(fontsize=8); plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUT,\"j4_pareto.png\"),dpi=110)\n142\tprint(\"\\nDONE j4\",flush=True)\n143\t"}]},"uuid":"c59eb2b0-48d5-4ad4-bf7b-ea1ccb61b53c","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:20:56.054Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e64e7c76-a6bb-4dd4-a139-d84fc5818ce4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"af6c8b58-5209-43a9-9ac5-fa066c21b11d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99f21099-1bdf-4e90-9d41-1443256357f6","agentId":"a37f3a34aafca097d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZMoeqeyt8VrXyJZCwritN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"\n2\tFeature-Resolved Attention (FRA) computation.\n3\t\n4\tProvides two entry points for computing 4-D FRA tensors:\n5\t  - ``get_sentence_fra_batch``: single-model SAE path\n6\t  - ``get_sentence_fra_crosscoder``: two-model crosscoder path\n7\t\n8\tBoth share the core tensor construction via ``_build_fra_result()``.\n9\t\"\"\"\n10\t\n11\timport math\n12\t\n13\timport numpy as np\n14\timport torch\n15\tfrom typing import Any, Dict\n16\tfrom einops import einsum\n17\tfrom tqdm import tqdm\n18\tfrom transformer_lens import HookedTransformer\n19\t\n20\tfrom fra.core.activations import get_llm_activations\n21\tfrom fra.core.helpers import get_W_K, apply_rope_to_projected, _extract_rope_params\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t# ── Top-k sparsification ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tdef topk_sparsify(\n28\t    feature_activations: torch.Tensor,\n29\t    top_k: int | None,\n30\t) -> torch.Tensor:\n31\t    \"\"\"Keep only top-k features per position by absolute activation magnitude.\n32\t\n33\t    Args:\n34\t        feature_activations: [seq_len, d_sae] tensor of feature activations.\n35\t        top_k: Number of features to keep per position.  None keeps all\n36\t               active (non-zero) features without truncation.\n37\t\n38\t    Returns:\n39\t        [seq_len, d_sae] tensor with at most top_k non-zero entries per row.\n40\t    \"\"\"\n41\t    if top_k is None:\n42\t        return feature_activations\n43\t\n44\t    seq_len = feature_activations.shape[0]\n45\t    topk_features = []\n46\t    for pos in range(seq_len):\n47\t        feat = feature_activations[pos]\n48\t        n_active = (feat != 0).sum().item()\n49\t\n50\t        if n_active > 0:\n51\t            k = min(top_k, n_active)\n52\t            _, topk_idx = torch.topk(feat.abs(), k)\n53\t            sparse_feat = torch.zeros_like(feat)\n54\t            sparse_feat[topk_idx] = feat[topk_idx]\n55\t        else:\n56\t            sparse_feat = torch.zeros_like(feat)\n57\t\n58\t        topk_features.append(sparse_feat)\n59\t\n60\t    return torch.stack(topk_features)\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t# ── Core FRA loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64\t\n65\t\n66\tdef compute_fra_sparse(\n67\t    topk_features: torch.Tensor,\n68\t    W_dec: torch.Tensor,\n69\t    W_Q: torch.Tensor,\n70\t    W_K: torch.Tensor,\n71\t    attn_scale: float,\n72\t    *,\n73\t    rms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n74\t    dec_norms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n75\t    rope_sin: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n76\t    rope_cos: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n77\t    rotary_dim: int | None = None,\n78\t    rotary_adjacent_pairs: bool = False,\n79\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n80\t    verbose: bool = False,\n81\t    layer_head_label: str = \"\",\n82\t) -> torch.sparse_coo_tensor:\n83\t    \"\"\"Compute the 4-D FRA sparse tensor from pre-computed feature activations.\n84\t\n85\t    All model-specific setup (activation extraction, encoding, weight lookup)\n86\t    happens in the caller; this function is the shared inner loop.\n87\t\n88\t    Args:\n89\t        topk_features: ``[seq_len, d_sae]`` already top-k sparsified.\n90\t        W_dec:  ``[d_sae, d_model]`` decoder weight matrix.\n91\t        W_Q:    ``[d_model, d_head]`` query projection for one head.\n92\t        W_K:    ``[d_model, d_head]`` key projection for one head.\n93\t        attn_scale: ``sqrt(d_head)`` scaling factor.\n94\t        rms:    Optional ``[seq_len]`` per-position RMS values for RMSNorm\n95\t                correction.  When provided, each interaction is divided by\n96\t                ``rms[query_idx] * rms[key_idx]``.\n97\t        dec_norms: Optional ``[d_sae]`` decoder-weight norms for SAEs\n98\t                trained with ``rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm=True``.\n99\t        rope_sin: Optional ``[n_ctx, rotary_dim]`` precomputed sine table\n100\t                from the attention block.  Pass for RoPE models (Gemma, Llama).\n101\t        rope_cos: Optional ``[n_ctx, rotary_dim]`` precomputed cosine table.\n102\t        rotary_dim: Number of RoPE dimensions (``model.cfg.rotary_dim``).\n103\t        rotary_adjacent_pairs: RoPE pair ordering flag from model config.\n104\t        chunk_size: Number of query positions per GPU batch before flushing\n105\t                to CPU.  Controls peak GPU memory.\n106\t        verbose: Show progress bar.\n107\t        layer_head_label: Label for progress bar (e.g. ``\"L5H3\"``).\n108\t\n109\t    Returns:\n110\t        ``torch.sparse_coo_tensor`` on CPU, shape\n111\t        ``[seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae]``, coalesced.\n112\t    \"\"\"\n113\t    seq_len = topk_features.shape[0]\n114\t    d_sae = topk_features.shape[1]\n115\t    shape = (seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae)\n116\t\n117\t    all_indices_cpu: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n118\t    all_values_cpu: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n119\t\n120\t    total_pairs = seq_len * (seq_len + 1) // 2\n121\t    pbar = tqdm(\n122\t        total=total_pairs,\n123\t        desc=f\"Computing FRA ({layer_head_label})\" if layer_head_label else \"Computing FRA\",\n124\t        disable=not verbose,\n125\t    )\n126\t\n127\t    for q_start in range(0, seq_len, chunk_size):\n128\t        q_end = min(q_start + chunk_size, seq_len)\n129\t        chunk_indices: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n130\t        chunk_values: list[torch.Tensor] = []\n131\t\n132\t        for query_idx in range(q_start, q_end):\n133\t            q_feat = topk_features[query_idx]\n134\t            q_active = torch.where(q_feat != 0)[0]\n135\t\n136\t            if len(q_active) == 0:\n137\t                pbar.update(query_idx + 1)\n138\t                continue\n139\t\n140\t            q_vecs = W_dec[q_active]                          # [n_q, d_model]\n141\t            q_proj = q_vecs @ W_Q                             # [n_q, d_head]\n142\t            q_scales = q_feat[q_active]                       # [n_q]\n143\t            if dec_norms is not None:\n144\t                q_scales = q_scales / dec_norms[q_active]\n145\t\n146\t            # Apply RoPE to query once per query position (outside key loop)\n147\t            if rope_sin is not None:\n148\t                q_proj = apply_rope_to_projected(\n149\t                    q_proj, query_idx, rope_sin, rope_cos,\n150\t                    rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n151\t                )\n152\t\n153\t            for key_idx in range(query_idx + 1):\n154\t                k_feat = topk_features[key_idx]\n155\t                k_active = torch.where(k_feat != 0)[0]\n156\t\n157\t                if len(k_active) == 0:\n158\t                    pbar.update(1)\n159\t                    continue\n160\t\n161\t                k_vecs = W_dec[k_active]                      # [n_k, d_model]\n162\t                k_proj = k_vecs @ W_K                         # [n_k, d_head]\n163\t\n164\t                # Apply RoPE to key for this key position\n165\t                if rope_sin is not None:\n166\t                    k_proj = apply_rope_to_projected(\n167\t                        k_proj, key_idx, rope_sin, rope_cos,\n168\t                        rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n169\t                    )\n170\t                k_scales = k_feat[k_active]                   # [n_k]\n171\t                if dec_norms is not None:\n172\t                    k_scales = k_scales / dec_norms[k_active]\n173\t\n174\t                int_matrix = (q_proj @ k_proj.T) / attn_scale  # [n_q, n_k]\n175\t                int_matrix = int_matrix * q_scales.unsqueeze(1) * k_scales.unsqueeze(0)\n176\t\n177\t                if rms is not None:\n178\t                    int_matrix = int_matrix / (rms[query_idx] * rms[key_idx])\n179\t\n180\t                mask = int_matrix.abs() > 1e-10\n181\t                if mask.any():\n182\t                    local_r, local_c = torch.where(mask)\n183\t                    n_int = len(local_r)\n184\t\n185\t                    pos_indices = torch.empty((4, n_int), dtype=torch.long)\n186\t                    pos_indices[0] = query_idx\n187\t                    pos_indices[1] = key_idx\n188\t                    pos_indices[2] = q_active[local_r].cpu()\n189\t                    pos_indices[3] = k_active[local_c].cpu()\n190\t\n191\t                    chunk_indices.append(pos_indices)\n192\t                    chunk_values.append(int_matrix[mask].detach().cpu().float())\n193\t\n194\t                pbar.update(1)\n195\t\n196\t        all_indices_cpu.extend(chunk_indices)\n197\t        all_values_cpu.extend(chunk_values)\n198\t\n199\t        device = topk_features.device\n200\t        if device.type != \"cpu\":\n201\t            torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n202\t\n203\t    pbar.close()\n204\t\n205\t    if all_indices_cpu:\n206\t        indices = torch.cat(all_indices_cpu, dim=1)\n207\t        values = torch.cat(all_values_cpu)\n208\t        fra_sparse = torch.sparse_coo_tensor(\n209\t            indices, values, size=shape, device=\"cpu\", dtype=torch.float32,\n210\t        ).coalesce()\n211\t    else:\n212\t        fra_sparse = torch.sparse_coo_tensor(\n213\t            torch.zeros((4, 0), dtype=torch.long),\n214\t            torch.zeros(0, dtype=torch.float32),\n215\t            size=shape, device=\"cpu\",\n216\t        )\n217\t\n218\t    return fra_sparse\n219\t\n220\t\n221\tdef _build_fra_result(\n222\t    model: HookedTransformer,\n223\t    layer: int,\n224\t    head: int,\n225\t    feature_activations: torch.Tensor,\n226\t    W_dec: torch.Tensor,\n227\t    device,\n228\t    *,\n229\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n230\t    rms_activations: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n231\t    dec_norms: torch.Tensor | None = None,\n232\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n233\t    verbose: bool = False,\n234\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n235\t    \"\"\"Shared post-encoding FRA construction.\n236\t\n237\t    Handles top-k sparsification, weight extraction, RMSNorm correction,\n238\t    RoPE, ``compute_fra_sparse``, device transfer, and result assembly.\n239\t\n240\t    Args:\n241\t        model: Target model (for W_Q / W_K and RoPE parameters).\n242\t        layer: Attention layer index.\n243\t        head: Attention head index.\n244\t        feature_activations: ``[seq, d_sae]`` raw encoded features.\n245\t        W_dec: ``[d_sae, d_model]`` decoder weights.\n246\t        device: Torch device for the result tensor.\n247\t        top_k: Features per position to keep (None = all).\n248\t        rms_activations: ``[seq, d_model]`` residual stream for RMSNorm\n249\t            correction, or None to skip.\n250\t        dec_norms: ``[d_sae]`` decoder norms for rescale correction, or None.\n251\t        chunk_size: GPU batch size for ``compute_fra_sparse``.\n252\t        verbose: Show progress.\n253\t\n254\t    Returns:\n255\t        Dict with ``fra_tensor_sparse``, ``shape``, ``seq_len``,\n256\t        ``total_interactions``, ``feature_activations``, ``topk_features``.\n257\t    \"\"\"\n258\t    topk_features = topk_sparsify(feature_activations, top_k).float()\n259\t\n260\t    # Attention weights — float32 for accumulation precision\n261\t    W_Q = model.blocks[layer].attn.W_Q[head].float()       # [d_model, d_head]\n262\t    W_K_mat = get_W_K(model, layer, head).float()           # [d_model, d_head]\n263\t    d_head = W_Q.shape[-1]\n264\t    attn_scale = math.sqrt(d_head)\n265\t\n266\t    # RMSNorm correction\n267\t    rms = None\n268\t    if rms_activations is not None:\n269\t        eps = model.cfg.eps\n270\t        rms = (rms_activations.float().pow(2).mean(dim=-1) + eps).sqrt()\n271\t\n272\t    # RoPE\n273\t    rope_sin, rope_cos, rotary_dim, rotary_adjacent_pairs = (\n274\t        _extract_rope_params(model, layer)\n275\t    )\n276\t\n277\t    fra_tensor_sparse = compute_fra_sparse(\n278\t        topk_features, W_dec.float(), W_Q, W_K_mat, attn_scale,\n279\t        rms=rms,\n280\t        dec_norms=dec_norms,\n281\t        rope_sin=rope_sin,\n282\t        rope_cos=rope_cos,\n283\t        rotary_dim=rotary_dim,\n284\t        rotary_adjacent_pairs=rotary_adjacent_pairs,\n285\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n286\t        verbose=verbose,\n287\t        layer_head_label=f\"L{layer}H{head}\",\n288\t    )\n289\t\n290\t    # Move to device if it fits\n291\t    if str(device) != \"cpu\":\n292\t        try:\n293\t            fra_tensor_sparse = fra_tensor_sparse.to(device)\n294\t        except RuntimeError:\n295\t            if verbose:\n296\t                print(\"Warning: sparse tensor too large for GPU, keeping on CPU.\")\n297\t\n298\t    seq_len = feature_activations.shape[0]\n299\t    d_sae = feature_activations.shape[-1]\n300\t    total_interactions = fra_tensor_sparse._nnz()\n301\t    shape = fra_tensor_sparse.shape\n302\t\n303\t    if verbose:\n304\t        _k = top_k if top_k is not None else d_sae\n305\t        density = total_interactions / max(seq_len * seq_len * _k * _k, 1)\n306\t        print(\n307\t            f\"4D FRA tensor: shape={shape}, \"\n308\t            f\"nnz={total_interactions:,}, density={density:.2%}\"\n309\t        )\n310\t\n311\t    return {\n312\t        \"fra_tensor_sparse\": fra_tensor_sparse,\n313\t        \"shape\": shape,\n314\t        \"seq_len\": seq_len,\n315\t        \"total_interactions\": total_interactions,\n316\t        \"feature_activations\": feature_activations,\n317\t        \"topk_features\": topk_features,\n318\t    }\n319\t\n320\t\n321\t# ── Legacy analysis helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────\n322\t\n323\t\n324\tdef lower_triangular_mask(pattern: np.ndarray) -> np.ma.MaskedArray:\n325\t    \"\"\"Apply lower triangular mask to attention pattern.\"\"\"\n326\t    mask = np.triu(np.ones(pattern.shape), k=1)\n327\t    return np.ma.array(np.tril(pattern, k=0), mask=mask)\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tdef attention_pattern_QK(llm: Any, layer: int, head: int, q_input: torch.Tensor,\n331\t                        q_do_bias: bool, k_input: torch.Tensor, k_do_bias: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n332\t    \"\"\"\n333\t    Compute attention pattern from query and key inputs.\n334\t\n335\t    Args:\n336\t        layer: Layer index\n337\t        head: Head index\n338\t        q_input: Query input tensor\n339\t        q_do_bias: Whether to add query bias\n340\t        k_input: Key input tensor\n341\t        k_do_bias: Whether to add key bias\n342\t\n343\t    Returns:\n344\t        Attention scores as numpy array\n345\t    \"\"\"\n346\t    W_Q = llm.blocks[layer].attn.W_Q[head]\n347\t    b_Q = llm.blocks[layer].attn.b_Q[head]\n348\t    W_K = llm.blocks[layer].attn.W_K[head]\n349\t    b_K = llm.blocks[layer].attn.b_K[head]\n350\t\n351\t    q = einsum(W_Q, q_input, \"d a, s d -> s a\")\n352\t    if q_do_bias:\n353\t        q += b_Q\n354\t\n355\t    k = einsum(W_K, k_input, \"d a, s d -> s a\")\n356\t    if k_do_bias:\n357\t        k += b_K\n358\t\n359\t    d_head = W_Q.shape[-1]\n360\t    attention_scores = einsum(q, k, \"q a, k a -> q k\") / math.sqrt(d_head)\n361\t\n362\t    return attention_scores.detach().cpu().numpy()\n363\t\n364\t\n365\tdef analyze_feature_attention_interactions(model: Any, sae: Any, layer: int, head: int,\n366\t                                           input_text: str, query_position: int, key_position: int,\n367\t                                           hook_point: str = \"hook_attn_out\") -> Dict:\n368\t    \"\"\"\n369\t    Analyze interactions between features in attention.\n370\t\n371\t    Args:\n372\t        layer: Layer index\n373\t        head: Head index\n374\t        input_text: Input text to analyze\n375\t        query_position: Query position\n376\t        key_position: Key position\n377\t    \"\"\"\n378\t    activations_SD = get_llm_activations(model,input_text,hook_point=hook_point,layers=layer)\n379\t    feature_activations_SH = sae.encode(activations_SD)\n380\t\n381\t    feature_activations_query = feature_activations_SH[query_position]\n382\t    query_active_features = torch.where(feature_activations_query != 0)[0]\n383\t\n384\t    feature_activations_key = feature_activations_SH[key_position]\n385\t    key_active_features = torch.where(feature_activations_key != 0)[0]\n386\t\n387\t    query_activations_for_features = sae.W_dec[query_active_features]\n388\t    key_activations_for_features = sae.W_dec[key_active_features]\n389\t\n390\t    interaction_matrix_unscaled = attention_pattern_QK(model, layer, head,\n391\t                                                        query_activations_for_features, False,\n392\t                                                        key_activations_for_features, False)\n393\t\n394\t\n395\t\n396\t    # Convert to numpy after using for indexing\n397\t    query_features_tensor = query_active_features\n398\t    key_features_tensor = key_active_features\n399\t\n400\t    matrix_scaling = feature_activations_query[query_features_tensor].unsqueeze(1) * \\\n401\t                    feature_activations_key[key_features_tensor].unsqueeze(0)\n402\t    matrix_scaling = matrix_scaling.detach().cpu().numpy()\n403\t\n404\t    query_active_features = query_features_tensor.cpu().numpy()\n405\t    key_active_features = key_features_tensor.cpu().numpy()\n406\t\n407\t    return {\n408\t        'query_active_features': query_active_features,\n409\t        'key_active_features': key_active_features,\n410\t        'interaction_matrix_unscaled': interaction_matrix_unscaled,\n411\t        'matrix_scaling': matrix_scaling,\n412\t        'interaction_matrix': interaction_matrix_unscaled * matrix_scaling\n413\t    }\n414\t\n415\t\n416\tdef get_sentence_averages(llm:Any,sae:Any,layer:int,head:int,input_text:str,hook_point:str=\"attn.hook_z\"):\n417\t\ttext_length=128\n418\t\thidden_dim=sae.d_sae\n419\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n420\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n421\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n422\t\tcount=0\n423\t\tfor key_index in tqdm(range(text_length), disable=True):\n424\t\t\tfor query_index in range(key_index,text_length):\n425\t\t\t\t\tfeature_analysis=analyze_feature_attention_interactions(llm,sae,layer,head,input_text,query_index,key_index,hook_point)\n426\t\t\t\t\tint_matrix=feature_analysis[\"interaction_matrix\"]\n427\t\t\t\t\tquery_active_features=feature_analysis[\"query_active_features\"]\n428\t\t\t\t\tkey_active_features=feature_analysis[\"key_active_features\"]\n429\t\t\t\t\tdata_independent=feature_analysis[\"interaction_matrix_unscaled\"]\n430\t\n431\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_int=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n432\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_int[query_active_features[:,None],key_active_features[None,:]]=int_matrix\n433\t\n434\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_localization=np.zeros((hidden_dim,hidden_dim))\n435\t\t\t\t\tresized_data_dependent_localization[query_active_features[:,None],key_active_features[None,:]]=np.abs(int_matrix)*(query_index-key_index)\n436\t\n437\t\n438\t\n439\t\n440\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix=data_dep_int_matrix+resized_data_dependent_int\n441\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs=data_dep_int_matrix_abs+np.abs(resized_data_dependent_int)\n442\t\t\t\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=data_dep_localization_matrix+resized_data_dependent_localization\n443\t\n444\t\t\t\t\tcount+=1\n445\t\n446\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix/=count\n447\t\tdata_dep_localization_matrix=data_dep_localization_matrix/np.clip(data_dep_int_matrix_abs,a_min=1,a_max=None)\n448\t\tdata_dep_int_matrix_abs/=count\n449\t\n450\t\treturn data_dep_int_matrix,data_dep_int_matrix_abs,data_dep_localization_matrix\n451\t\n452\t\n453\t\n454\t\n455\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n456\t# Entry point: single-model SAE path\n457\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n458\t\n459\t\n460\t@torch.no_grad()\n461\tdef get_sentence_fra_batch(\n462\t    model: HookedTransformer,\n463\t    sae: Any,\n464\t    text: str,\n465\t    layer: int,\n466\t    head: int,\n467\t    max_length: int = 128,\n468\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n469\t    verbose: bool = False,\n470\t    hook_point: str = \"ln1.hook_normalized\",\n471\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n472\t    normalize_by_decoder_norm: bool | None = None,\n473\t    prepend_bos: bool | None = None,\n474\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n475\t    \"\"\"\n476\t    Compute full 4D Feature-Resolved Attention tensor for a sentence.\n477\t    Returns a sparse representation to avoid memory issues.\n478\t\n479\t    hook_point controls which activation the SAE was trained on:\n480\t      - \"ln1.hook_normalized\"  (default, correct for FRA): decoder vectors live in\n481\t        the same d_model space that W_Q / W_K project from.  This is the only\n482\t        mathematically correct choice.\n483\t      - \"attn.hook_z\"          (legacy, for pre-trained hook_z SAEs): decoder\n484\t        vectors are in concatenated-heads space, not d_model space; the QK\n485\t        attention score computation is therefore approximate.\n486\t\n487\t    Args:\n488\t        model: The transformer model\n489\t        sae: The SAE (any object with .encode() and .W_dec attributes)\n490\t        text: Input text to analyze\n491\t        layer: Which layer to analyze\n492\t        head: Which attention head to analyze\n493\t        max_length: Maximum sequence length\n494\t        top_k: Number of top features to keep per position\n495\t        verbose: Whether to show progress\n496\t        hook_point: Hookpoint the SAE was trained on (relative to blocks.{layer}.)\n497\t        chunk_size: Number of query positions to process per GPU batch before\n498\t                    flushing results to CPU.  Reduce for large SAEs (e.g. Gemma-Scope)\n499\t                    to avoid GPU OOM.  Set to seq_len to process everything at once.\n500\t        normalize_by_decoder_norm: Whether to divide feature activations by\n501\t                    decoder weight norms to match SAEs trained with\n502\t                    rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm=True.  None (default) auto-detects\n503\t                    from the SAE config.  True/False forces the behaviour.\n504\t        prepend_bos: Whether to include special tokens (BOS) in tokenization.\n505\t                    None (default) uses the tokenizer's default behaviour.\n506\t                    True/False forces add_special_tokens on/off.\n507\t\n508\t    Returns:\n509\t        Dictionary containing:\n510\t            - fra_tensor_sparse: Sparse 4D tensor indices and values\n511\t            - shape: Shape of the full tensor [seq_len, seq_len, d_sae, d_sae]\n512\t            - seq_len: Actual sequence length\n513\t            - total_interactions: Total number of non-zero interactions\n514\t            - normalized: Whether decoder-norm normalization was applied\n515\t    \"\"\"\n516\t    device = next(model.parameters()).device\n517\t\n518\t    # Tokenise and truncate\n519\t    if prepend_bos is not None:\n520\t        tokens = model.tokenizer.encode(text, add_special_tokens=prepend_bos)\n521\t    else:\n522\t        tokens = model.tokenizer.encode(text)\n523\t    if max_length is not None and len(tokens) > max_length:\n524\t        tokens = tokens[:max_length]\n525\t\n526\t    tokens_tensor = torch.tensor(tokens).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n527\t    hook_name = f\"blocks.{layer}.{hook_point}\"\n528\t    _, cache = model.run_with_cache(tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name])\n529\t\n530\t    act = cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)  # remove batch dim\n531\t\n532\t    # hook_z is [seq_len, n_heads, d_head] → flatten to [seq_len, n_heads*d_head]\n533\t    # ln1.hook_normalized is already [seq_len, d_model]\n534\t    if act.dim() == 3:\n535\t        act = act.flatten(-2, -1)\n536\t\n537\t    # Encode to SAE features\n538\t    if verbose:\n539\t        print(f\"Encoding {act.shape[0]} positions to SAE features...\")\n540\t\n541\t    if hasattr(sae, 'encode'):\n542\t        feature_activations = sae.encode(act)   # [seq_len, d_sae]\n543\t    else:\n544\t        feature_activations = sae.sae.encode(act)\n545\t\n546\t    # If the SAE normalizes inputs (e.g. Gemma-Scope), the feature activations\n547\t    # are in the normalized scale.  Divide by the norm coefficient so that\n548\t    # FRA[q,k,i,j] sums to the actual (un-normalized) QK attention score.\n549\t    # Top-k ranking is unaffected (same scalar per position).\n550\t    if hasattr(sae, '_norm_coeff') and sae._norm_coeff is not None:\n551\t        feature_activations = feature_activations / sae._norm_coeff\n552\t\n553\t    # Get decoder weights\n554\t    if hasattr(sae, 'W_dec'):\n555\t        W_dec = sae.W_dec   # [d_sae, d_model]\n556\t    else:\n557\t        W_dec = sae.sae.W_dec\n558\t\n559\t    # Handle rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm: when the SAE was trained with this\n560\t    # flag, encode() returns activations scaled UP by ||W_dec[i]||, and decode()\n561\t    # scales them back DOWN.  The true per-feature contribution to x is\n562\t    #   (f[i] / ||W_dec[i]||) * W_dec[i]\n563\t    # but without correction FRA would use f[i] * W_dec[i], inflating each\n564\t    # entry by ||W_dec[q_feat]|| * ||W_dec[k_feat]||.\n565\t    if normalize_by_decoder_norm is None:\n566\t        inner = sae.sae if hasattr(sae, 'sae') else sae\n567\t        cfg = getattr(inner, 'cfg', None)\n568\t        do_normalize = getattr(cfg, 'rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm', False) if cfg else False\n569\t    else:\n570\t        do_normalize = normalize_by_decoder_norm\n571\t\n572\t    if do_normalize:\n573\t        dec_norms = W_dec.norm(dim=-1)  # [d_sae]\n574\t        if verbose:\n575\t            print(\"Applying decoder-norm correction (rescale_acts_by_decoder_norm)\")\n576\t    else:\n577\t        dec_norms = None\n578\t\n579\t    # RMSNorm correction is needed when the SAE's decoder vectors live in\n580\t    # residual-stream space but W_Q / W_K project from post-RMSNorm space.\n581\t    # Use the full reconstructed activations (not actual model activations)\n582\t    # so that FRA scores match coder-patched scores when all features are kept.\n583\t    if \"resid\" in hook_point:\n584\t        b_dec = sae.b_dec\n585\t        x_hat = feature_activations @ W_dec + b_dec\n586\t        rms_activations = x_hat\n587\t    else:\n588\t        rms_activations = None\n589\t\n590\t    result = _build_fra_result(\n591\t        model, layer, head, feature_activations, W_dec, device,\n592\t        top_k=top_k,\n593\t        rms_activations=rms_activations,\n594\t        dec_norms=dec_norms,\n595\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n596\t        verbose=verbose,\n597\t    )\n598\t    result[\"normalized\"] = do_normalize\n599\t    return result\n600\t\n601\t\n602\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n603\t# Entry point: two-model crosscoder path\n604\t# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n605\t\n606\t\n607\t@torch.no_grad()\n608\tdef get_sentence_fra_crosscoder(\n609\t    base_model: HookedTransformer,\n610\t    it_model: HookedTransformer,\n611\t    crosscoder: Any,\n612\t    tokens: list,\n613\t    head: int = 0,\n614\t    crosscoder_layer: int = 13,\n615\t    max_length: int = 128,\n616\t    top_k: int | None = 20,\n617\t    verbose: bool = False,\n618\t    chunk_size: int = 16,\n619\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n620\t    \"\"\"Compute 4-D FRA tensor using a model-diffing crosscoder.\n621\t\n622\t    The crosscoder was trained on ``hook_resid_post`` at ``crosscoder_layer``.\n623\t    That residual stream state is the input to the *next* layer's attention\n624\t    (``hook_resid_pre`` at ``crosscoder_layer + 1``), so we always analyse\n625\t    attention at ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.  The same activations are used\n626\t    for crosscoder encoding and for the RMSNorm correction.\n627\t\n628\t    The attention layer is **not** independently configurable — it is always\n629\t    ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.  This ensures the FRA decomposition corresponds\n630\t    to the features the crosscoder actually learned.\n631\t\n632\t    Args:\n633\t        base_model:  HookedTransformer for model-index 0 (base).\n634\t        it_model:    HookedTransformer for model-index 1 (instruct).\n635\t        crosscoder:  ``GemmaCrosscoderFRA`` instance.\n636\t        tokens:      Token IDs to analyse.  Caller is responsible for\n637\t                     tokenization (including chat template if needed).\n638\t        head:        Attention head index.\n639\t        crosscoder_layer:\n640\t            Layer from which to extract residual-stream activations for the\n641\t            crosscoder (default 13, matching the published checkpoint).\n642\t            Uses ``hook_resid_post`` at this layer.  The attention layer\n643\t            is derived as ``crosscoder_layer + 1``.\n644\t        max_length:  Maximum sequence length.\n645\t        top_k:       Keep only top-k features per position.\n646\t        verbose:     Show progress bar.\n647\t        chunk_size:  Query positions per GPU batch (controls peak memory).\n648\t\n649\t    Returns:\n650\t        Dict with keys:\n651\t          - ``fra_tensor_sparse``  (torch.sparse_coo_tensor, 4-D)\n652\t          - ``shape``\n653\t          - ``seq_len``\n654\t          - ``total_interactions``\n655\t          - ``feature_activations``  (torch.Tensor, [seq, d_sae])\n656\t          - ``topk_features``  (torch.Tensor, [seq, d_sae])\n657\t    \"\"\"\n658\t    layer = crosscoder_layer + 1\n659\t    target_model = base_model if crosscoder.model_idx == 0 else it_model\n660\t    other_model = it_model if crosscoder.model_idx == 0 else base_model\n661\t    device = next(target_model.parameters()).device\n662\t\n663\t    # Truncate if needed\n664\t    if max_length is not None and len(tokens) > max_length:\n665\t        tokens = tokens[:max_length]\n666\t    tokens_tensor = torch.tensor(tokens).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n667\t\n668\t    # Extract activations from both models at crosscoder_layer\n669\t    hook_name = f\"blocks.{crosscoder_layer}.hook_resid_post\"\n670\t\n671\t    _, target_cache = target_model.run_with_cache(\n672\t        tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name],\n673\t    )\n674\t    _, other_cache = other_model.run_with_cache(\n675\t        tokens_tensor, names_filter=[hook_name],\n676\t    )\n677\t\n678\t    target_act = target_cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)      # [seq, d_model]\n679\t    other_act = other_cache[hook_name].squeeze(0)\n680\t\n681\t    # Stack in crosscoder order: [base, instruct]\n682\t    if crosscoder.model_idx == 0:\n683\t        x_stacked = torch.stack([target_act, other_act], dim=1)\n684\t    else:\n685\t        x_stacked = torch.stack([other_act, target_act], dim=1)\n686\t\n687\t    # Encode through crosscoder\n688\t    if verbose:\n689\t        print(f\"Encoding {target_act.shape[0]} positions through crosscoder...\")\n690\t    feature_activations = crosscoder.encode(x_stacked)   # [seq, d_sae]\n691\t\n692\t    # Crosscoder decoder vectors live in residual-stream space, so RMSNorm\n693\t    # correction is always needed.  Use the full reconstructed activations\n694\t    # (not actual model activations) so that FRA scores match coder-patched\n695\t    # scores when all features are kept.\n696\t    #\n697\t    # Decode in float32 to match the precision used for per-feature W_dec\n698\t    # projections inside compute_fra_sparse (which casts W_dec.float()).\n699\t    # Using the native float16 decode would introduce precision mismatch\n700\t    # between the RMS denominator and the per-feature numerators.\n701\t    b_dec_rms = crosscoder.b_dec.float().to(device)\n702\t    x_hat = feature_activations.float() @ crosscoder.W_dec.float() + b_dec_rms\n703\t    return _build_fra_result(\n704\t        target_model, layer, head, feature_activations, crosscoder.W_dec, device,\n705\t        top_k=top_k,\n706\t        rms_activations=x_hat,\n707\t        chunk_size=chunk_size,\n708\t        verbose=verbose,\n709\t    )\n710\t\n711\t\n712\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n713\t    print('main character')\n714\t"}]},"uuid":"c1b3ebee-a25b-46a2-b4a2-d3c979fed172","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:21:00.731Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"af6c8b58-5209-43a9-9ac5-fa066c21b11d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
